und no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay fixtures are synthetic flat messages, not recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 requires replaying recorded PI corpora and states M0 corpora are fixture inputs (`stories/03-capture-verification.md:6`, `:13`, `:24`, `:28`, `:33`). The fixture contract says `test/fixtures/corpus.ts` should load M0 captures, while synthetic builders are for lifecycle and turn-derivation tests (`tech-design.md:557-560`). Current `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4` states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, and each named loader constructs `source` from `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` / `makeToolResult` rather than loaded recorded hook events (`corpus.ts:21-29`, `:42-53`, `:69-83`, `:97-105`, `:118-124`). The replay harness type is `source: AgentMessage[]` (`src/verify/replay.ts:39-42`) and it reconstructs lifecycle by inferring `agent_end` before a fresh user prompt and stamping synthetic entry IDs (`src/verify/replay.ts:111-147`). A filesystem search found no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"TC-6.1 mechanical replay p