ual `dispose()` method on `LhcInstance`, but `initInstance` currently returns `ok:false`, so no runtime instance exists whose dispose method can be invoked. The smoke test in `packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:86-92` only invokes `initInstance` and asserts `not_implemented`; it does not invoke or prove a dispose seam.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:758:        - \"S0-FIXTURE-HARNESS: corpus, synthetic, model-call, and temp-thread fixtures exist; corpus validation rejects malformed fixtures; temp-thread tests create and reopen real SQLite-backed LHC threads.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:761:        - \"S0-SMOKE-INIT-DISPOSE: dispose side of the stubbed lifecycle seam is not callable or tested as fail-closed.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:776:      - \"`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` currently builds synthetic stand-ins for the named corpora. I treated that as non-blocking for Story 0 because `team-impl-log.md` records M0 real recorded corpus breadth as Story 3 fixture scope.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:809:      {\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg --files'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"pnpm-workspace.yaml\\nAGENTS.md\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/assignments.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/startup-validation.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/shared/instance.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/shared/diagnostics.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/shared/not-implemented.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\\npackages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\\npackages/p