/threads.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-thread.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-boundary.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/corrupt.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/work-handlers.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/fixtures/receipt-schema.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/view-select-golden.test.ts\\npackages/lhc/test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts\\npackages/lhc/reference/src-green-thread-events-v1/index.ts\\ndocs/key-insights/meta-thinking-and-tensions-braindump.md\\npackages/lhc/reference/src-green-thread-events-v1/token-counting/local-token-counter.ts\\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\\ndocs/onboard/02-domain-design.md\\ndocs/onboard/01-core-concepts.md\\n\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:439:    planSummary: \"Built the pi-lhc walking skeleton (Epic 1 Chunk 0, tdd-lite, observe-only). Scaffolded the package (package.json with lhc workspace dep + verification-tier scripts, tsconfig/tsconfig.test mirroring lhc, vitest config, and zero-dep lint/boundaries/immutability scripts incl. a new connector-specific check-boundaries.mjs enforcing pinned cross-surface import edges for lifecycle/capture/inference/verify with no cycle). Declared the PI v0.79.2 extension surface locally in src/pi/types.ts (the @earendil-works PI packages are not installed in this workspace) from the verified wiring research. src/index.ts registers exactly the 9-hook Epic 1 observe-only rail (NOT context) via activate(pi)/createConnector(), with guarded handlers that never throw into PI and retain only plain data. lifecycle/state.ts is complete plain-data SessionState (the anti-stale-ctx shape) + createSessionState; every other module is a typed fail-closed stub per the tech-design Interface Definitions — pure algorithms (mapMessage, eventKey, TurnAccumulator, classifyFailure, detectFork, validateReachable, report, loadAssignments) throw NotImplementedError, services (initInstance, resolveThread, pickThread, capture, seedFork) return an LHC not_implemented OpResult, createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other' failure, and replayCorpus returns matches:false — no stub reports success. initLhc is provided as the createSdk rename (A-4). Test fixtures: corpus loader (5 named lifecycles) with a real validateCorpus shape/coherence checker + makeTruncatedCorpus, synthetic PI/intake builders, deterministic ModelCall fakes, and a real temp-SQLite-thread factory. 6 foundation test files / 19 tests cover corpus validity (+ invalid builder rejected), synthetic coherence, ModelCall fakes, temp-thread create+reopen, hook-rail registration + fail-closed/plain-data handlers + init/dispose seam, and verification-config presence.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:476:        reason: \"Fail-closed primitives: NotImplementedError (pure-algo stubs) + notImplemented OpResult using LHC's not_implemented code (service stubs).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:485:        reason: \"COMPLETE (not stubbed) plain-data SessionState + createSessionState + CaptureFailureDiagnostic — the shape that makes PI-context retention impossible (AC-1.3/2.7).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:491:        reason: \"LaunchFlags interface + fail-closed resolveThread stub.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:494:        reason: \"Fail-closed pickThread stub (--resume picker).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:500:        reason: \"MapCtx interface + mapMessage pure stub (throws NotImplementedError).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:503:        reason: \"mapModelSelect/mapThinkingLevelSelect pure stubs (throw).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:506:        reason: \"TurnAccumulator pure state-machine stub (throws).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:509:        reason: \"eventKey pure stub (throws).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:512:        reason: \"Fail-closed capture() orchestrator stub.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:515:        reason: \"createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other'-failure function (never success); classifyFailure pure stub (throws).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:518:        reason: \"loadAssignments stub (throws; never returns a placeholder map).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:521:        reason: \"ValidationReport re-export (spec'd home) + validateReachable/report stubs (throw).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:526:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:533:        reason: \"Deterministic ModelCall fakes: fakeModelCallText/fakeModelCallFailure/fakeModelCallRouter.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:541:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:545:        reason: \"ModelCall fakes well-formed: text, each failure kind, router routing + fail-closed on unrouted key.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:561:        - \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:588:        - \"Held the anti-shim line on the two factory/result stubs that are easy to fake: createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other' failure (never ok:true) and replayCorpus returns matches:false — neither reports success.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:596:      - \"Q3 (tech design): M0 recorded-corpora breadth — the corpus loaders build synthetic stand-ins for the 5 named lifecycles and the machinery widens as real recordings arrive (Story 3).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:597:      - \"Q1/A-7 (tech design): image/file-reference intake handling is an M0 decision; the safe interim is degrade-to-runtime_note, which the converter implements in Story 2.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:667:      - \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:668:      - \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:673:    reviewScopeSummary: \"Verified Story 0 foundation scope against the story, full connector-core tech design, test plan, implementor artifact, pi-lhc source, fixture tests, smoke tests, package scripts, and fresh gates. Most foundation evidence is present, but the required callable dispose half of the stubbed init/dispose seam is not implemented or tested.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:681:        evidence: \"Story 0 requires the stubbed init/dispose seam to be callable and return typed fail-closed results. In `packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts:12-24`, only `initLhc` and fail-closed `initInstance` are exported. `packages/pi-lhc/src/shared/instance.ts:12-15` declares an eventual `dispose()` method on `LhcInstance`, but `initInstance` currently returns `ok:false`, so no runtime instance exists whose dispose method can be invoked. The smoke test in `packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:86-92` only invokes `initInstance` and asserts `not_implemented`; it does not invoke or prove a dispose seam.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:696:        evidence: \"Story 0 requires the stubbed init/dispose seam to be callable and return typed fail-closed results. In `packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts:12-24`, only `initLhc` and fail-closed `initInstance` are exported. `packages/pi-lhc/src/shared/instance.ts:12-15` declares an eventual `dispose()` method on `LhcInstance`, but `initInstance` currently returns `ok:false`, so no runtime instance exists whose dispose method can be invoked. The smoke test in `packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts:86-92` only invokes `initInstance` and asserts `not_implemented`; it does not invoke or prove a dispose seam.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:713:        - \"S0-FIXTURE-HARNESS: corpus, synthetic, model-call, and temp-thread fixtures exist; corpus validation rejects malformed fixtures; temp-thread tests create and reopen real SQLite-backed LHC threads.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:716:        - \"S0-SMOKE-INIT-DISPOSE: dispose side of the stubbed lifecycle seam is not callable or tested as fail-closed.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:731:      - \"`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` currently builds synthetic stand-ins for the named corpora. I treated that as non-blocking for Story 0 because `team-impl-log.md` records M0 real recorded corpus breadth as Story 3 fixture scope.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:27:Build the walking skeleton for the pi-lhc extension: package scaffold, PI hook registration rail, plain-data-only state holder, stubbed LHC init/dispose seam, corpus fixture loader, and typed fail-closed stubs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:34:**Objective:** Establish the loadable extension structure every later story builds on, with no stale PI context retained across hook boundaries and no stub that can fake successful capture.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:42:- Typed fail-closed stubs for unimplemented capture, inference, validation, and fork behavior.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:78:- This is foundation work with no AC owner, but later stories can be reward-hacked if stubs fake success.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:92:| Capture/inference/fork stubs | `packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/*`, `packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/*`, `packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:93:| Fixtures | `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/thread.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:108:| None | `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts`, extension-load smoke, package script checks | Foundation has no story-owned TC; smoke checks prove load, hook rail, fail-closed stubs, fixture validity, and verification-script availability. |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:120:- Keep `state.ts` complete rather than stubbed: it is the shape that prevents stale PI context retention later.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:124:- No stub may report successful capture, derivation, validation, fork seeding, or replay before the owning story implements it.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:165:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:211:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:212:| TC-2.8 *(risk: atomicity)* | Malformed→gap vs store-unavailable→health signal | (a) malformed on writable thread; (b) unavailable store | (a) durable queryable gap; (b) extension health signal in `SessionState.health`, no gap, no hook exception |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:213:| TC-2.9 | Model/thinking changes captured as ordered runtime_notes | fire `model_select` then `thinking_level_select` mid-sequence | each records one `runtime_note` carrying new+previous value; order preserved relative to surrounding messages |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:250:| TC-4.1 | Function resolves (provider,model) via registry, returns text | fake registry + complete returning text | returns `{ok:true,text}` for a single-turn message list |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:251:| TC-4.2 | Two kinds → different (provider,model) both route in one session | two assignments, two fakes | each call routes by its keys; both succeed |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:253:| TC-4.4 | Resolved-but-no-output → `empty_output` by adapter (not host fn) | complete returns empty content | LHC adapter yields `empty_output`; host fn returns text-or-transport-failure only |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:259:| TC-4.5 | Captured thread's queued derivation invokes fn + persists outcome | captured thread; fakes (one text, one failure); `drainSettled` | at least one ready derived form + one classified failure, both queryable via inspect/health |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:276:| TC-5.6 | Incomplete/unknown assignment fails loud at init | missing kind / unknown prompt / placeholder | construction throws actionable error; no placeholder masks it |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:284:| TC-6.3 | inspect overview/health reflect captured session | a captured thread with a gap + a failed form | counts, last position, gaps, failed derivations all visible |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:296:Each chunk: write skeletons (structured-result stubs for services/adapters/handlers; `NotImplementedError` for pure algorithms) → Red (tests written, failing for the right reason — never asserting on `NotImplementedError`) → Green (implement to pass). Exit each chunk on `green-verify`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:300:- **Skeleton:** all interface exports (`tech-design.md` → Interface Definitions); `index.ts` hook registration with stubbed handlers; `state.ts` complete (plain data, no stub).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:301:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:307:- **Skeleton:** `instance.ts`, `thread-resolution.ts`, `picker.ts` as structured-result stubs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:314:- **Skeleton:** `map-message.ts`, `turn-accumulator.ts`, `idempotency.ts` (`NotImplementedError`); `converter.ts` (structured result).\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:316:- **Green:** mapping fan-out, turn accumulation, runtime-change capture (model/thinking → runtime_note), key construction, batch flush with failure isolation.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:359:No suite is skipped on auth availability — the closed-loop test (TC-4.5) uses a deterministic `ModelCall` fake, not a live provider, so it always runs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:424:        - \"S0-DOD-INIT-DISPOSE: stubbed LHC init/dispose seam is callable and fail-closed.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:444:      - \"The new dispose seam remains fail-closed and does not create a fake usable LHC instance.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:484:    planSummary: \"Built the pi-lhc walking skeleton (Epic 1 Chunk 0, tdd-lite, observe-only). Scaffolded the package (package.json with lhc workspace dep + verification-tier scripts, tsconfig/tsconfig.test mirroring lhc, vitest config, and zero-dep lint/boundaries/immutability scripts incl. a new connector-specific check-boundaries.mjs enforcing pinned cross-surface import edges for lifecycle/capture/inference/verify with no cycle). Declared the PI v0.79.2 extension surface locally in src/pi/types.ts (the @earendil-works PI packages are not installed in this workspace) from the verified wiring research. src/index.ts registers exactly the 9-hook Epic 1 observe-only rail (NOT context) via activate(pi)/createConnector(), with guarded handlers that never throw into PI and retain only plain data. lifecycle/state.ts is complete plain-data SessionState (the anti-stale-ctx shape) + createSessionState; every other module is a typed fail-closed stub per the tech-design Interface Definitions — pure algorithms (mapMessage, eventKey, TurnAccumulator, classifyFailure, detectFork, validateReachable, report, loadAssignments) throw NotImplementedError, services (initInstance, resolveThread, pickThread, capture, seedFork) return an LHC not_implemented OpResult, createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other' failure, and replayCorpus returns matches:false — no stub reports success. initLhc is provided as the createSdk rename (A-4). Test fixtures: corpus loader (5 named lifecycles) with a real validateCorpus shape/coherence checker + makeTruncatedCorpus, synthetic PI/intake builders, deterministic ModelCall fakes, and a real temp-SQLite-thread factory. 6 foundation test files / 19 tests cover corpus validity (+ invalid builder rejected), synthetic coherence, ModelCall fakes, temp-thread create+reopen, hook-rail registration + fail-closed/plain-data handlers + init/dispose seam, and verification-config presence.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:521:        reason: \"Fail-closed primitives: NotImplementedError (pure-algo stubs) + notImplemented OpResult using LHC's not_implemented code (service stubs).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:530:        reason: \"COMPLETE (not stubbed) plain-data SessionState + createSessionState + CaptureFailureDiagnostic — the shape that makes PI-context retention impossible (AC-1.3/2.7).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:536:        reason: \"LaunchFlags interface + fail-closed resolveThread stub.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:539:        reason: \"Fail-closed pickThread stub (--resume picker).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:545:        reason: \"MapCtx interface + mapMessage pure stub (throws NotImplementedError).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:548:        reason: \"mapModelSelect/mapThinkingLevelSelect pure stubs (throw).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:551:        reason: \"TurnAccumulator pure state-machine stub (throws).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:554:        reason: \"eventKey pure stub (throws).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:557:        reason: \"Fail-closed capture() orchestrator stub.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:560:        reason: \"createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other'-failure function (never success); classifyFailure pure stub (throws).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:563:        reason: \"loadAssignments stub (throws; never returns a placeholder map).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:566:        reason: \"ValidationReport re-export (spec'd home) + validateReachable/report stubs (throw).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:571:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:578:        reason: \"Deterministic ModelCall fakes: fakeModelCallText/fakeModelCallFailure/fakeModelCallRouter.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:586:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:590:        reason: \"ModelCall fakes well-formed: text, each failure kind,