-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/state.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/validate.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"manual node --input-type=module reload redelivery reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist/index.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"manual node --input-type=module malformed-gap inspect.health reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist and packages/lhc/dist\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"manual node --input-type=module unsupported toolResult fileRef mapping check\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"reviewScopeSummary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Initial verification covered Story 2 AC/TC requirements, Flow 2 tech design, production capture/idempotency/failure paths, Story 2 tests, configured gates, and targeted manual reproductions for reload redelivery, health surfacing, and unsupported content handling.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"priorFindingStatuses\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"newFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"critical\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reload/crash-replay redelivery records duplicates instead of skipping them\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AC-2.6 and TC-2.7 require redelivered reload/replay events to be skipped by the same idempotency key. The production connector seeds captureSession.sourceSeq from inspect.overview event count on session_start (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:312-326), then generates new entry ids from that counter for message/runtime hooks (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:364-378). TurnAccumulator likewise seeds turn_end keys from closed turn count (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts:35-62). Because eventKey gives entryId first precedence (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-44), a redelivered historical message after reload gets a new key instead of the original key. Manual reproduction against built production code: after recording user_prompt 'first' and turn_end, a reload redelivering the same user message produced four stored events [user_prompt, turn_end, user_prompt, turn_end] with keys s0/turn:0 and s2/turn:1; connector diagnostic was null. Existing reattach tests prove new post-resume messages record, but do not prove reload/crash-replay historical redelivery skips.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-2.7\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Writable capture gaps are not surfaced in thread health\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed/unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap that surfaces in thread health. capture() records the gap as a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts:48-56) and connector state records lastCaptureFailure (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:344-358), but inspect health is composed only from message/turn form reports (packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-108). The current test asserts only listEvents contains a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:149-158), not inspect.health. Manual reproduction after capture([malformed turn_end]) showed the runtime_note gap in listEvents, while inspect.health returned owners=[], failures=[], repairPreview=[], queue={queued:0,claimed:0}.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-2.8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Atomicity / Isolation\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-003\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Unsupported tool-result content parts are silently omitted\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The story risk reminders and tech design require unsupported image/file-reference parts to record an omission rather than vanish silently. map-message.ts defines unsupportedOf/omissionText and uses them for user and assistant messages (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:52-61, 131-168), but mapToolResult only joins text parts and emits one tool_result (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:185-197). Manual mapMessage({role:'toolResult', toolCallId:'call_file', content:[{type:'fileRef', path:'/tmp/out.png'}]}) returned only tool_result with content:'' and no runtime_note omission.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TechDesign-I-6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Production Path Audit\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"same-session-implementor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"openFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"critical\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reload/crash-replay redelivery records duplicates instead of skipping them\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AC-2.6 and TC-2.7 require redelivered reload/replay events to be skipped by the same idempotency key. The production connector seeds captureSession.sourceSeq from inspect.overview event count on session_start (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:312-326), then generates new entry ids from that counter for message/runtime hooks (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:364-378). TurnAccumulator likewise seeds turn_end keys from closed turn count (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts:35-62). Because eventKey gives entryId first precedence (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-44), a redelivered historical message after reload gets a new key instead of the original key. Manual reproduction against built production code: after recording user_prompt 'first' and turn_end, a reload redelivering the same user message produced four stored events [user_prompt, turn_end, user_prompt, turn_end] with keys s0/turn:0 and s2/turn:1; connector diagnostic was null. Existing reattach tests prove new post-resume messages record, but do not prove reload/crash-replay historical redelivery skips.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-2.7\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Writable capture gaps are not surfaced in thread health\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed/unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap that surfaces in thread health. capture() records the gap as a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts:48-56) and connector state records lastCaptureFailure (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:344-358), but inspect health is composed only from message/turn form reports (packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-108). The current test asserts only listEvents contains a runtime_note (packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:149-158), not inspect.health. Manual reproduction after capture([malformed turn_end]) showed the runtime_note gap in listEvents, while inspect.health returned owners=[], failures=[], repairPreview=[], queue={queued:0,claimed:0}.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-2.8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Atomicity / Isolation\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-003\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Unsupported tool-result content parts are silently omitted\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The story risk reminders and tech design require unsupported image/file-reference parts to record an omission rather than vanish silently. map-message.ts defines unsupportedOf/omissionText and uses them for user and assistant messages (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:52-61, 131-168), but mapToolResult only joins text parts and emits one tool_result (packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:185-197). Manual mapMessage({role:'toolResult', toolCallId:'call_file', content:[{type:'fileRef', path:'/tmp/out.png'}]}) returned only tool_result with content:'' and no runtime_note omission.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TechDesign-I-6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Production Path Audit\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"same-session-implementor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"requirementCoverage\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"verified\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1 happy-path user, assistant, and toolResult capture in source order with assistant thinking -> text -> tool_call fan-out.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 / TC-2.3 PI per-step turn_end is ignored, LHC turn_end is emitted at agent_end, and repeated turnIndex values do not drive ordering.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4 parallel tool results carry toolCallId and preserve out-of-order arrival without arrival-order correlation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5 error tool result captures content with isError true.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6 graceful interrupt captures partial assistant content, carries aborted disposition, and closes the turn at agent_end.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9 model_select and thinking_level_select are captured as ordered runtime_note events with previous and new values.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Direct same-key capture() batch reflush dedups through LHC intakeStream and returns skipped duplicate_idempotency_key outcomes.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Story gate pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify passed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic gate pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all passed.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"unverified\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7 production hook-level reload and crash-replay redelivery: manual reproduction shows duplicates, not skips.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8 thread-health surfacing for durable writable capture gaps: manual reproduction shows inspect.health does not report the gap.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TechDesign-I-6 unsupported image/file-reference omission coverage for toolResult messages: code audit and manual mapper call show omission is not recorded.\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\"gatesRun\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"manual node --input-type=module reload redelivery reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist/index.js\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fail\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"manual node --input-type=module malformed-gap inspect.health reproduction against packages/pi-lhc/dist and packages/lhc/dist\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fail\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Production connector idempotency currently uses attach-time event/turn counts as the generated entry-id seed; that fixes normal resume append collisions but breaks reload/crash-replay redelivery dedup by assigning historical events new keys.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Writable-thread capture failure is persisted as a runtime_note but is not represented in LHC inspect.health, so the durable gap is queryable only as a generic event log entry, not as thread health.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"mapToolResult silently drops non-text fileRef/image parts because unsupported-part omission handling is only implemented for user and assistant messages.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"No material fake/mock intake path was found in Story 2 capture execution; production capture writes through real LHC intakeStream.messageEvents. Test fakes are confined to fixtures/config.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"revise\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fresh-fix-path\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"openQuestions\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"additionalObservations\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Configured gates pass with 58 tests, but the required reload/crash-replay and health-surfacing scenarios are not covered by those tests.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/008-verify.json exists but is zero bytes; this verification did not rely on it.\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\"errors\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"artifacts\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"result-envelope\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/008-verify.json\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"startedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-14T08:23:55.717Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finishedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-14T08:59:32.802Z\\\\\\\"}\\\\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json:1:{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"story-verify\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"needs-user-decision\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"needs-human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"resultId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"9717c2cb-c337-418c-9476-1f6c2c9146b8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"story_verifier\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"gpt-5.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sessionId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"019ec4a2-e6a9-7261-a8a1-c863991dc47a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"continuation\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"sessionId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"019ec4a2-e6a9-7261-a8a1-c863991dc47a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"storyId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"mode\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"followup\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"story\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Story 1: Session Lifecycle and Thread Resolution\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"artifactsRead\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"reviewScopeSummary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Follow-up verification focused on prior SV-001 and SV-002 plus directly touched lifecycle surfaces. The configured gates pass, and the module-scope reload memory was removed, but both prior blockers now depend on explicit spec deviations that require human ruling before the story can pass.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"priorFindingStatuses\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"needs-human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The module-scope thread id was removed, but reload for no-flag and --resume now reattaches to the cwd's most-recent registry row rather than reconstructing from the resolved thread id required by AC-1.5. The implementor artifact and code both identify this as an Epic-1 convenience with a known concurrent same-cwd limitation and defer precise lineage to Feature 2+.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"needs-human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The production path now shows the cwd-scoped title/created/id list through ctx.ui.notify, but it still auto-selects the most recent thread. AC-1.7 requires resolving the operator's selection; the implementor records this as a spec deviation because PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive selection surface.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"newFindings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"openFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Reload reconstruction still does not use the resolved thread id for no-flag and --resume reloads\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id (story lines 51-53). The revised resolveReloadThread handles --session by id, but for no-flag and --resume it lists threads by cwd and chooses listed.value.at(-1) at packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:118-147. The implementor artifact records that a concurrent same-cwd session could be selected instead and defers precise reload lineage to Feature 2+. The test at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:335-370 proves only the single-thread-in-cwd case, not reconstruction from the prior resolved thread id.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.5\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"SV-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Production --resume still does not resolve an operator selection\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"AC-1.7 requires --resume/-r to list cwd-scoped threads with title and creation time and resolve the operator's selection (story lines 59-61; tech design lines 231 and 251-253). The revised defaultSelectThread shows the list via ctx.ui.notify but then returns mostRecent.threadId at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:157-176. The production test asserts notification plus most-recent behavior at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255-290. The implementor artifact records this as a spec deviation because the available PI UI surface has notify but no interactive input.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.7\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.7\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"requirementCoverage\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"verified\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1 / TC-1.1: no-flag session_start creates one cwd/title registry thread and one background LHC instance; lifecycle tests and pi-lhc verify pass.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.2 / TC-1.2: existing --session launch attaches to the existing thread and creates no second thread.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.3 / TC-1.3 plain-data holder: connector snapshot remains structuredClone-able across fresh ctx objects.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.4 / TC-1.4: shutdown dispose flush preserves pre-shutdown intake events across re-resolve.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.6 / TC-1.6: launch modes and bad/ambiguous id behavior remain covered.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"A-8 registry support remains covered by lhc threads-a8 focused test.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"unverified\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.5 / TC-1.5 for no-flag and --resume reload reconstruction from the resolved thread id; current implementation uses cwd-most-recent registry selection.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.7 / TC-1.7 production operator selection; current implementation presents choices but auto-selects most recent.\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\"gatesRun\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pnpm --filter lhc exec vitest run test/threads-a8.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Reload production path for no-flag/--resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection, not the prior 