ontext/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 2 against AC-2.1 through AC-2.8, TC-2.1 through TC-2.9, current capture source/tests, production capture paths, LHC duplicate-key behavior, and configured gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id, no-position capture events still collide on fallback idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded and AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events. The local production hook type keeps both MessageEndEvent.entryId and MessageEndEvent.position optional in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-39. The hook path only supplies fallbackId from event.position when entryId is absent in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:379-385, and runtime-change hooks do the same for optional position in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:402-415. If position is absent, eventKey falls to fallbackId \\\"no-stable-id\\\" in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:54-60. Focused checks failed: two no-entryId/no-position same-text user prompts produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:user:user_prompt:2cda7449dd14dbba9a0c9de9`, and two identical model_select events without position produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:system:runtime_note:fad453e343e63228f9ea2f15`. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events on this production path can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id, no-position capture events still collide on fallback idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized PI message to be recorded and AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events. The local production hook type keeps both MessageEndEvent.entryId and MessageEndEvent.position optional in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-39. The hook path only supplies fallbackId from event.position when entryId is absent in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:379-385, and runtime-change hooks do the same for optional position in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:402-415. If position is absent, eventKey falls to fallbackId \\\"no-stable-id\\\" in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:54-60. Focused checks failed: two no-entryId/no-position same-text user prompts produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:user:user_prompt:2cda7449dd14dbba9a0c9de9`, and two identical model_select events without position produced the identical key `pi:s:fp:no-stable-id:0:system:runtime_note:fad453e343e63228f9ea2f15`. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events on this production path can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: user/assistant/toolResult source-order capture and assistant thinking -> text -> tool_call fan-out are covered through the real hook -> converter -> LHC intake path in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:43-87.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: the worked example records exactly one LHC turn_end at agent_end and PI per-step turn_end hooks produce none in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:39-83.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.3: two runs with repeated turnIndex 0 order by converter source-event order in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:86-118.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4: parallel out-of-order tool results correlate by toolCallId in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:39-77.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5: tool result isError and error content are captured without drop in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:80-105.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6: graceful interrupt partial content, aborted disposition runtime_note, and complete-but-aborted turn close are covered in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:29-65.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: stable-key re-delivery skips and normal resume without historical re-fire are covered for entryId/source-position-backed cases in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:145-191 and packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:138-168.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: malformed writable-thread input records a durable capture gap surfaced in health, unavailable store records health signal with no thrown hook exception, and unmappable hook input records a gap in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:140-276.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: model_select and thinking_level_select produce ordered runtime_note events with previous/new values in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:90-137.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.1 / AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: distinct no-entryId/no-position same-content message_end events are not safely recorded; focused evidence shows duplicate fallback idempotency keys.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: repeated identical runtime-selection events without position are not safely recorded; focused evidence shows duplicate fallback idempotency keys.\",\"Required proof that PI always supplies entryId or position to the production hooks is absent from the story, tech design, research evidence read, and local types; the implemented absent-position path remains live.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec tsx -e 'mapMessage two same-text no-entryId/no-position user prompts must produce distinct keys'\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec tsx -e 'mapModelSelect two identical no-position runtime changes must produce distinct keys'\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts relies on optional event.position as the only fallback discriminator when entryId is absent; packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts does not require that field, and packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts collapses the absent-position path to `no-stable-id`, causing duplicate-key skips in LHC intake.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured story and epic gates pass: 14 test files / 68 tests passed in each gate run.\",\"Prior unmappable-hook gap and multiple unsupported tool-result omission key issues are covered by current code/tests and were not reopened in this initial verification.\",\"No material fake adapter, mock path, shim, or placeholder was found in the Story 2 capture production path; later-story fail-closed inference stubs remain outside this story's capture scope.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/012-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T10:27:14.496Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T10:33:05.228Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-story-orchestrate-resume.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate resume\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"completed\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyId\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHistoryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\",\"finalPackagePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"finalPackage\":{\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyRunId\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution-story-run-001\",\"storyId\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\",\"attempt\":1,\"summary\":{\"storyTitle\":\"Story 1: Session Lifecycle and Thread Resolution\",\"implementedScope\":\"Addressed verifier 011 findings SV-001 and SV-002 only, preserving the resolved SV-003 title work, production activate path, fail-closed observeOnlyProvider, and A-8 registry changes. SV-001 (reload used in-process memory): removed the module-scope rememberedSessionThreadId entirely — along with resetSessionThreadMemory, threadIdOf, and launchFor — and made reload re-resolve the thread from DURABLE registry state via a new resolveReloadThread in thread-resolution.ts. On reload, --session/--continue re-resolve by their durable launch input (idempotent, never creating), and a no-flag or --resume session reattaches to the cwd's most-recently-created thread read from the registry (listThreads({cwd}).at(-1)); it never creates a duplicate and never re-prompts. The connector now holds no module-level or durable handoff state; reattach is keyed on the session_start reason (reload vs not), and onDispose no longer keeps/clears any reload memory. This makes the durable reload source the LHC registry (the catalog), not a PI-session->thread mapping or recovery sidecar (epic I-1), answering the verifier's open question. SV-002 (production --resume bypassed operator selection): defaultSelectThread now PRESENTS the cwd-scoped titled candidate list (title + creation time + id, via a renderResumeCandidates helper) through ctx.ui.notify when ctx.hasUI, then resolves to the most-recently-created thread as the best available explicit default — PI v0.79.2 exposes only ui.notify, no interactive input surface — while picker.ts stays cwd-scoped, titled, and selection-injectable (pickThread's select seam). Tests: the reload describe block now proves a fresh connector with an empty closure reattaches purely from the registry (no module handoff, no duplicate), plus a --session reload re-resolve test and a reason-driven 'new always creates' test; the architecture-risk resolve-by-durable-id-after-discard primitive remains. The production --resume tests now assert the operator-visible presentation (cwd-scoped, titled, with creation time, via ctx.ui.notify) and a headless-safe path (no notify when hasUI:false, still resolves). resetSessionThreadMemory was removed from instance.test.ts, thread-resolution.test.ts, and the smoke test; the red-manifest was re-recorded for the two verifier-directed frozen lifecycle files. All pi-lhc gates (verify, green-verify incl. immutability, verify-all) and lhc verify pass.\",\"acceptanceRationale\":\"Story-lead is pausing for caller ruling 01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution-story-run-001-ruling-048 before impl-lead can accept the story.\"},\"evidence\":{\"implementorArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/003-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/010-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"selfReviewArtifacts\":[],\"verifierArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/004-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/011-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"quickFixArtifacts\":[],\"callerInputArtifacts\":[],\"gateRuns\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter lhc exec vitest run test/threads-a8.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"}]},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"block\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/011-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\",\"AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id (story lines 51-53). The revised resolveReloadThread handles --session by id, but for no-flag and --resume it lists threads by cwd and chooses listed.value.at(-1) at packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:118-147. The implementor artifact records that a concurrent same-cwd session could be selected instead and defers precise reload lineage to Feature 2+. The test at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:335-370 proves only the single-thread-in-cwd case, not reconstruction from the prior resolved thread id.\"]},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/011-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\",\"AC-1.7 requires --resume/-r to list cwd-scoped threads with title and creation time and resolve the operator's selection (story lines 59-61; tech design lines 231 and 251-253). The revised defaultSelectThread shows the list via ctx.ui.notify but then returns mostRecent.threadId at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:157-176. The production test asserts notification plus most-recent behavior at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255-290. The implementor artifact records this as a spec deviation because the available PI UI surface has notify but no interactive input.\"]}]},\"riskAndDeviationReview\":{\"specDeviations\":[{\"description\":\"Production --resume operator selection: PI v0.79.2 exposes ctx.ui.notify but NO interactive input/selection surface (wiring research). The production picker therefore PRESENTS the cwd-scoped titled candidate list (title + creation time + id) via ctx.ui.notify when ctx.hasUI and resolves to the most-recently-created thread as the best available explicit default; resuming a SPECIFIC thread is done with --session <id> (full or partial). The picker stays cwd-scoped, titled, and selection-injectable (pickThread's select seam, exercised by tests); a true interactive picker is deferred to a PI input surface.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/003-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/010-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"needs-ruling\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"Reload reconstruction source: reload re-resolves the thread from the durable LHC registry (the catalog), not from a PI-session->thread mapping record or recovery sidecar (epic I-1). For no-flag/--resume reload the reattach target is the cwd's most-recently-created thread; for --session/--continue it is the launch input re-resolved by id. An Epic-1 convenience with a known cross-process-same-cwd limitation; the permanent home for reload lineage is LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+).\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/003-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/010-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"needs-ruling\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"(inherited, preserved) Local PI extension types in src/pi/types.ts (Story 0 accepted-risk); initLhc thin wrapper over createSdk (A-4); resolveThread/pickThread injected-deps signatures vs the interface sketch; Story-1 production inference is the fail-closed observeOnlyProvider placeholder (real PI-auth-backed inference is Stories 5/6); new threads created with cwd + a default title equal to the cwd leaf; A-8 LHC additions (ambiguous_thread_id, registry v2 cwd migration) land in this story's scope.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/003-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/010-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json\"],\"approvalSt