on/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/index.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/state-machine.ts\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 2 against AC-2.1 through AC-2.8, TC-2.1 through TC-2.9, current capture source, capture tests, LHC intake behavior, health surfacing, and configured pi-lhc gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide on idempotency keys\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.1 requires every finalized message to be recorded, AC-2.6 requires duplicate safety without dropping distinct events, and tech-design.md:329 requires fallback keys to be identical for the same logical re-delivery and distinct across different events using role/timestamp/content-hash. The implemented fallback in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:38-60 uses fallbackId default \\\"no-stable-id\\\", blockIndex, role, kind, and content, with no timestamp or source-event ordinal. Production message routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 may call mapMessage with only piSessionId when PI provides no entryId, and runtime-change routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:362-373 always passes only piSessionId. Focused checks showed mapMessage for two no-entryId user prompts with the same text returns the same key, and mapModelSelect for two identical runtime changes returns the same key. LHC skips duplicate keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216, so later distinct events can be skipped.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unmappable PI hook input records no durable gap on writable threads\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed or unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap surfaced in health. The production hook path maps before capture: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 calls mapMessage, then accumulator.onMessage, then capture. mapMessage has no default case at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:232-240; a focused check with role \\\"bogus\\\" returned undefined. That means onMessageEnd throws before capture can write a gap, and the generic guard at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:385-400 converts the failure into a recordedGap:false diagnostic. The existing TC-2.8 test covers a malformed MessageEventInput passed directly to capture at packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:135-178, not an unmappable PI message through the real hook path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Multiple unsupported tool-result parts share one omission key\",\"evidence\":\"Story risk reminder at 02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md:88-91 says unsupported image/file-reference parts must record an omission. mapToolResult iterates unsupported parts and emits one runtime_note per part at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:223-227, but each call includes the same toolCallId. eventKey then takes the toolCallId branch at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:47-49 and ignores blockIndex/content, so two omission runtime_notes for the same tool result get the same key. A focused mapMessage check for a toolResult with fileRef a.bin and b.bin produced two runtime_note events with identical key `pi:thread-1:tool:call_1:runtime_note`; LHC's duplicate-key skip path at packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216 means the later omission is not recorded.\",\"affectedFi