-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Unmappable PI hook input records no durable gap on writable threads\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.7 and TC-2.8 require a malformed or unmappable event on a writable thread to record a durable, queryable gap surfaced in health. The production hook path maps before capture: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-357 calls mapMessage, then accumulator.onMessage, then capture. mapMessage has no default case at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:232-240; a focused check with role \\\"bogus\\\" returned undefined. That means onMessageEnd throws before capture can write a gap, and the generic guard at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:385-400 converts the failure into a recordedGap:false diagnostic. The existing TC-2.8 test covers a malformed MessageEventInput passed directly to capture at packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:135-178, not an unmappable PI message through the real hook path.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-003\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Multiple unsupported tool-result parts share one omission key\",\"evidence\":\"Story risk reminder at 02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation.md:88-91 says unsupported image/file-reference parts must record an omission. mapToolResult iterates unsupported parts and emits one runtime_note per part at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts:223-227, but each call includes the same toolCallId. eventKey then takes the toolCallId branch at packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:47-49 and ignores blockIndex/content, so two omission runtime_notes for the same tool result get the same key. A focused mapMessage check for a toolResult with fileRef a.bin and b.bin produced two runtime_note events with identical key `pi:thread-1:tool:call_1:runtime_note`; LHC's duplicate-key skip path at packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216 means the later omission is not recorded.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"Story Risk Reminder: unsupported content omission\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1 / TC-2.1: covered for a user/assistant/toolResult sequence with assistant fan-out thinking -> text -> tool_call in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:43-87.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2: covered for the worked example; PI per-step turn_end hooks produce no LHC turn_end and agent_end emits one close in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:39-83.\",\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.3: covered for two runs each using turnIndex 0, ordered by source-event order in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/turn-derivation.test.ts:86-118.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.4: covered for parallel tool results arriving b then a and correlated by toolCallId in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:39-77.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.5: covered for isError tool results preserving error flag and content in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:80-105.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.6: covered for graceful interrupt partial content, aborted disposition runtime_note, and closed turn in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:29-65.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.7: covered for same-key re-delivery skip and normal resume no historical re-fire in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:126-172 and packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts:138-168.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: covered for malformed LHC intake event direct-to-capture gap and unavailable store health signal in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:124-218.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: covered for a single model_select and thinking_level_select sequence producing ordered runtime_note events with new and previous values in packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts:90-121.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.1 / AC-2.6: distinct no-entryId same-content messages are not safely recorded because fallback idempotency keys collide.\",\"AC-2.8 / TC-2.9: repeated identical runtime changes are not safely recorded because runtime_note fallback keys collide.\",\"AC-2.7 / TC-2.8: unmappable PI hook input on a writable thread is not proven to record a durable gap; code evidence shows it becomes a recordedGap:false diagnostic before capture writes anything.\",\"Story risk reminder for unsupported image/file-reference omissions: multiple unsupported parts in one tool result are not safely recorded because omission runtime_notes share a key.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapMessage same no-entryId user prompts produce distinct keys\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapModelSelect repeated identical runtime changes produce distinct keys\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapMessage invalid role produces a durable writable-thread gap path\",\"result\":\"fail\"},{\"command\":\"focused: mapMessage two unsupported tool-result parts produce distinct omission keys\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts fallback keys can collide for distinct no-id messages and runtime changes, causing LHC duplicate-key skips in production capture.\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts handles unmappable PI message failures through the generic hook guard before capture can write a durable gap on a writable thread.\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts emits duplicate idempotency keys for multiple unsupported tool-result omission runtime_notes under the same toolCallId.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured story and epic gates both pass, so the blocking issues are coverage/behavior gaps not gate failures.\",\"No material fake adapter, mock path, shim, or placeholder was found in the Story 2 capture production path; later-story NotImplemented modules remain out of Story 2 scope.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/02-event-capture-and-turn-derivation/011-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T09:48:49.627Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T09:53:27.297Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/007-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"01a3e81d-90a1-4cc8-85a8-22e6d9b9e34c\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5ea-fdf4-73e1-a3aa-8057551be95e\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5ea-fdf4-73e1-a3aa-8057551be95e\",\"storyId\":\"03-capture-verification\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-capture-verification\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Capture Verification\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/03-capture-verification.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/003-implementor.json\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Verified Story 3 against AC-6.1 through AC-6.3, the replay harness, fixture loaders, replay tests, supporting capture path, current artifacts, and configured gates. The replay mechanics and gates pass, but the required recorded PI corpus proof is still missing because the fixture substrate uses synthetic stand-ins and inferred lifecycle.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay fixtures are synthetic flat messages, not recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 requires replaying recorded PI corpora and states M0 corpora are fixture inputs (`stories/03-capture-verification.md:6`, `:13`, `:24`, `:28`, `:33`). The fixture contract says `test/fixtures/corpus.ts` should load M0 captures, while synthetic builders are for lifecycle and turn-derivation tests (`tech-design.md:557-560`). Current `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4` states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, and each named loader constructs `source` from `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` / `makeToolResult` rather than loaded recorded hook events (`corpus.ts:21-29`, `:42-53`, `:69-83`, `:97-105`, `:118-124`). The replay harness type is `source: AgentMessage[]` (`src/verify/replay.ts:39-42`) and it reconstructs lifecycle by inferring `agent_end` before a fresh user prompt and stamping synthetic entry IDs (`src/verify/replay.ts:111-147`). A filesystem search found no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay fixtures are synthetic flat messages, not recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 requires replaying recorded PI corpora and states M0 corpora are fixture inputs (`stories/03-capture-verification.md:6`, `:13`, `:24`, `:28`, `:33`). The fixture contract says `test/fixtures/corpus.ts` should load M0 captures, while synthetic builders are for lifecycle and turn-derivation tests (`tech-design.md:557-560`). Current `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4` states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, and each named loader constructs `source` from `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` / `makeToolResult` rather than loaded recorded hook events (`corpus.ts:21-29`, `:42-53`, `:69-83`, `:97-105`, `:118-124`). The replay harness type is `source: AgentMessage[]` (`src/verify/replay.ts:39-42`) and it reconstructs lifecycle by inferring `agent_end` before a fresh user prompt and stamping synthetic entry IDs (`src/verify/replay.ts:111-147`). A filesystem search found no recorded corpus artifacts beyond `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` and `corpus.test.ts`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\",\"AC-6.2\",\"TC-6.2\",\"DoD-fixture-replay-M0-corpora\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"TC-6.1 mechanical replay path for current loaders: `replayCorpus` drives `mapMessage` -> `TurnAccumulator` -> `capture`, then compares durable events, `messages.listMessages`, and `turns.listTurns` (`src/verify/replay.ts:117-152`, `:432-457`).\",\"TC-6.2 mechanical determinism for current loaders: replay tests compare two fresh-thread logical event read-backs and same-thread re-replay dedup behavior (`test/verify/replay.test.ts:96-129`).\",\"TC-6.3 inspect surfaces: replay tests assert overview counts, last event position, failed derivations, and a capture gap visible through health (`test/verify/replay.test.ts:132-200`).\",\"Fixture-validity risk test for current fixtures: `validateCorpus` checks event shapes, tool-result correlation, closed turn, and rejects `makeTruncatedCorpus` (`test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts`).\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1 recorded PI corpus input: current named corpora are synthetic stand-ins, not M0 recorded PI captures.\",\"AC-6.2 / TC-6.2 deterministic replay over recorded corpora: determinism is proven only over synthetic `AgentMessage[]` fixtures with inferred lifecycle.\",\"Definition of Done: fixture replay for all available M0 corpora is not established because no M0 recorded corpus artifacts are loaded.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/verify/replay.test.ts test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"F-03-001: Story 3's verification proof path still relies on synthetic fixture stand-ins and inferred lifecycle rather than recorded PI hook corpus fixtures.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"openQuestions\":[\"Are the M0 recorded PI corpus artifacts available outside the current workspace? They are not present in the repository paths inspected.\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"The previous shallow compare concern is closed in the current code: `replayCorpus` now reads and compares `messages.listMessages` and `turns.listTurns`, not only event counts or overview counts.\",\"No Story 3 runtime path was found that serves context to a model; the replay provider fails closed and health assertions verify failed derivations are visible.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/007-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:36:12.327Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:40:01.223Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-continue\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"7c262b39-11f7-4587-b0a8-ed3911efd99a\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"fc8b0d70-702e-4abc-9faa-dda18cc81eaf\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"fc8b0d70-702e-4abc-9faa-dda18cc81eaf\",\"storyId\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Session Lifecycle and Thread Resolution\"},\"planSummary\":\"Addressed verifier 011 findings SV-001 and SV-002 only, preserving the resolved SV-003 title work, production activate path, fail-closed observeOnlyProvider, and A-8 registry changes. SV-001 (reload used in-process memory): removed the module-scope rememberedSessionThreadId entirely — along with resetSessionThreadMemory, threadIdOf, and launchFor — and made reload re-resolve the thread from DURABLE registry state via a new resolveReloadThread in thread-resolution.ts. On reload, --session/--continue re-resolve by their durable launch input (idempotent, never creating), and a no-flag or --resume session reattaches to the cwd's most-recently-created thread read from the registry (listThreads({cwd}).at(-1)); it never creates a duplicate and never re-prompts. The connector now holds no module-level or durable handoff state; reattach is keyed on the session_start reason (reload vs not), and onDispose no longer keeps/clears any reload memory. This makes the durable reload source the LHC registry (the catalog), not a PI-session->thread mapping or recovery sidecar (epic I-1), answering the verifier's open question. SV-002 (production --resume bypassed operator selection): defaultSelectThread now PRESENTS the cwd-scoped titled candidate list (title + creation time + id, via a renderResumeCandidates helper) through ctx.ui.notify when ctx.hasUI, then resolves to the most-recently-created thread as the best available explicit default — PI v0.79.2 exposes only ui.notify, no interactive input surface — while picker.ts stays cwd-scoped, titled, and selection-injectable (pickThread's select seam). Tests: the reload describe block now proves a fresh connector with an empty closure reattaches purely from the registry (no module handoff, no duplicate), plus a --session reload re-resolve test and a reason-driven 'new always creates' test; the architecture-risk resolve-by-durable-id-after-discard primitive remains. The production --resume tests now assert the operator-visible presentation (cwd-scoped, titled, with creation time, via ctx.ui.notify) and a headless-safe path (no notify when hasUI:false, still resolves). resetSessionThreadMemory was removed from instance.test.ts, thread-resolution.test.ts, and the smoke test; the red-manifest was re-recorded for the two verifier-directed frozen lifecycle files. All pi-lhc gates (verify, green-verify incl. immutability, verify-all) and lhc verify pass.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"reason\":\"Add resolveReloadThread: reload reconstruction from durable registry state (--session/--continue re-resolve by durable launch input; no-flag/--resume reattach to the cwd's most-recently-created thread via listThreads({cwd})), never creating and never re-prompting; returns null when the cwd has no thread to reattach.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"SV-001: remove module-scope rememberedSessionThreadId, resetSessionThreadMemory, threadIdOf, and launchFor; route reload session_start through resolveReloadFor (registry-based reattach) keyed on event.reason, add buildResolveDeps, simplify onDispose (no handoff state). SV-002: defaultSelectThread now presents the cwd-scoped titled candidates via ctx.ui.notify when ctx.hasUI (new renderResumeCandidates helper) and resolves to most-recent as the best available default. Update the activate() doc accordingly.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Remove resetSessionThreadMemory; rewrite the reload describe block to prove durable registry-based reattach with a fresh empty-closure connector, plus a --session reload re-resolve test and a reason-driven 'new always creates' test; rewrite the production --resume tests to assert the operator-visible ctx.ui.notify presentation (cwd-scoped, titled, with creation time) and a headless-safe path.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Remove the now-deleted resetSessionThreadMemory import and beforeEach call (no module-level connector state remains to reset).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Remove the now-deleted resetSessionThreadMemory import and beforeEach call.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"Re-record sha256 hashes for the two verifier-directed frozen lifecycle test files (instance.test.ts, thread-resolution.test.ts) so check-test-immutability matches their updated, strengthened content.\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: 'TC-1.7 production --resume is headless-safe' (no notify when hasUI:false, still resolves)\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: 'reload reattaches by re-resolving --session from the registry' (durable id evidence, creates nothing)\"],\"modified\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: reload describe block rewritten (fresh-connector durable registry reattach; 'new always creates' replaces the old memory-clearing test); production --resume test rewritten to assert the ctx.ui.notify operator-visible presentation; resetSessionThreadMemory removed\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts: resetSessionThreadMemory import + beforeEach call removed (case count unchanged)\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts: resetSessionThreadMemory import + beforeEach call removed (case count unchanged)\"],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":384,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":3},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"SV-001: removed module-scope rememberedSessionThreadId (and resetSessionThreadMemory/threadIdOf/launchFor); reload now re-resolves from the durable LHC registry via resolveReloadThread — --session/--continue by durable launch input, no-flag/--resume reattach to the cwd's most-recently-created registry row — never creating a duplicate or re-prompting; the connector keeps no module-level handoff and reattach is keyed on session_start reason. TC-1.5 rewritten so a fresh connector with an empty closure reattaches purely from the registry; added a --session reload test and a reason-driven 'new always creates' test; the resolve-by-durable-id-after-discard architecture-risk primitive remains.\",\"SV-002: production --resume presents the cwd-scoped titled candidate list (title + creation time + id) through ctx.ui.notify when ctx.hasUI, then resolves to the most-recent as the best available explicit default (PI v0.79.2 has no interactive input surface); picker.ts stays cwd-scoped, titled, and selection-injectable. Tests assert the operator-visible presentation and a headless-safe path.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"The durable reload source is the LHC registry (the catalog), NOT a PI-session->thread mapping or recovery sidecar — honoring epic I-1 and answering the verifier's open question.\",\"Reload reattach for no-flag/--resume uses the cwd's most-recently-created thread; within a single Story-1 session that is this session's thread. A concurrent session creating a newer thread in the same cwd could be reattached instead — an Epic-1 limitation; the permanent home for reload/fork lineage is LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+).\",\"Reattach is reload-only, keyed on the session_start reason (reload vs not), not on any retained memory; a reason:new no-flag session always creates a new thread.\",\"Re-recording the red-manifest was required because the verifier directed the test updates; the rewritten frozen tests strengthen coverage (durable-registry reattach + operator-visible picker), they do not weaken it.\"]},\"openQuestions\":[\"Concurrent same-cwd sessions: a no-flag/--resume reload resolves the cwd's most-recent thread, which could be a sibling session's newer thread. A precise per-session durable thread identity (LHC thread metadata, Feature 2+) or a PI-provided stable session key would remove this edge.\",\"Which PI selection surface enables a TRUE interactive --resume operator picker? PI v0.79.2 exposes only ctx.ui.notify; confirm against the real @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent dependency when it becomes a build dep, then replace the notify-list + most-recent default.\",\"(carried) Exact PI launch-flag spelling for --session (recon notes --session-id); title derivation strategy beyond the cwd-leaf interim (TDQ Q4).\"],\"specDeviations\":[\"Production --resume operator selection: PI v0.79.2 exposes ctx.ui.notify but NO interactive input/selection surface (wiring research). The production picker therefore PRESENTS the cwd-scoped titled candidate list (title + creation time + id) via ctx.ui.notify when ctx.hasUI and resolves to the most-recently-created thread as the best available explicit default; resuming a SPECIFIC thread is done with --session <id> (full or partial). The picker stays cwd-scoped, titled, and selection-injectable (pickThread's select seam, exercised by tests); a true interactive picker is deferred to a PI input surface.\",\"Reload reconstruction source: reload re-resolves the thread from the durable LHC registry (the catalog), not from a PI-session->thread mapping record or recovery sidecar (epic I-1). For no-flag/--resume reload the reattach target is the cwd's most-recently-created thread; for --session/--continue it is the launch input re-resolved by id. An Epic-1 convenience with a known cross-process-same-cwd limitation; the permanent home for reload lineage is LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+).\",\"(inherited, preserved) Local PI extension types in src/pi/types.ts (Story 0 accepted-risk); initLhc thin wrapper over createSdk (A-4); resolveThread/pickThread injected-deps signatures vs the interface sketch; Story-1 production inference is the fail-closed observeOnlyProvider placeholder (real PI-auth-backed inference is Stories 5/6); new threads created with cwd + a default title equal to the cwd leaf; A-8 LHC additions (ambiguous_thread_id, registry v2 cwd migration) land in this story's scope.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation) on the lifecycle/instance seam. Separately, when @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent becomes a build dependency, confirm the launch-flag spelling and whether a richer PI selection surface enables a true interactive --resume picker (replacing the notify-list + most-recent default), and revisit reload thread-identity precision via LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+) to close the concurrent-same-cwd edge.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/013-continue.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T05:48:04.803Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T06:03:46.600Z\"}\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:2:// fixtures (synthetic.ts, thread.ts) this is test infrastructure, not a test:\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:6:// tech design fixes them — the PI hook surface is fed synthetic events, and the\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:23:import { makeSessionStart } from \"../fixtures/synthetic.js\";\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:29:export function syntheticCtx(cwd = \"/work/capture\"): ExtensionContext {\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:35:    sessionManager: { getEntries: () => [] },\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/support.ts:85:  const ctx = syntheticCtx(cwd);\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/003-epic-review.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Canonical review uses the single reviewer result from epic-reviewer-2.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2, 4, 5, and 6 are mostly coherent: capture, turn derivation, fork replay, inference routing, and startup validation all run through connector entry points and real LHC surfaces.\",\"Story 1 thread identity drift remains material: the current code both adds a PI custom-entry thread pointer and still keeps a cwd-most-recent fallback, while the epic and tech design describe launch/registry resolution with no PI-session-to-thread mapping.\",\"Story 3 does not meet the epic-level verification contract because the corpus loaders are synthetic stand-ins rather than recorded PI corpora.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Epic 1 correctly remains observe-only: index.ts registers no context hook and capture does not alter what PI serves to the model.\",\"The converter architecture matches the tech design: map-message is pure, turn-accumulator owns the LHC turn boundary, and converter writes through intakeStream.messageEvents.\",\"The current reload implementation conflicts with the tech design resolution of I-1/I-7: tech-design.md says there is no stored PI-session-to-thread pointer, but index.ts writes and reads a pi-lhc-thread-state custom entry via appendEntry/sessionManager.\",\"The production --resume default does not resolve an operator selection. It notifies the candidate list, auto-resolves only one candidate, and returns null for multiple candidates.\",\"Fork seeding uses the real intake path and source read-back is not written, but the fork path uses a filePath ThreadRef for the target, which is another sign that lifecycle thread identity is not consistently registry-id based.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Flow 1 is incomplete against the written architecture and AC-1.7: launch resolution exists, but reload identity and resume selection still require human ruling or design update.\",\"Flow 2 is covered by source and tests: ordered message mapping, turn derivation, runtime notes, idempotency, gaps, parallel tools, errors, and aborts are implemented.\",\"Flow 3 is implemented with replay seeding and derived-form requeue; source immutability is covered.\",\"Flow 4 is implemented through createModelCall over PI modelRegistry plus pi-ai dynamic import, with classified failures and closed-loop persisted outcomes covered.\",\"Flow 5 is implemented: assignments load defaults/overrides, startup validation reports unreachable lanes, and capture continues.\",\"Flow 6 is not fully covered: replay is deterministic and compares real read-back, but it consumes synthetic fixtures instead of recorded PI corpora required by AC-6.1.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapter was found in src capture/fork/inspect paths: capture uses real LHC intakeStream, fork replay uses intakeStream.messageEvents, and inspect reads real LHC surfaces.\",\"Test-only model fakes are confined to test/fixtures and are not production code.\",\"createModelCall does not fabricate output when pi-ai is missing; it returns a classified failure.\",\"Material non-real verification path: packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts explicitly says loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, so Flow 6 is not proving recorded PI corpus replay.\",\"Material architecture drift: production index.ts persists threadRef in PI custom entries, despite tech-design.md stating the mapping persistence problem is dissolved and no session-file pointer is written.\",\"Material resume limitation: production defaultSelectThread has no interactive operator selection path for multiple cwd-scoped threads.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Capture verification uses synthetic stand-ins instead of recorded PI corpora\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:69 and epic.md:229-231 require recorded corpora replay through the converter. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-5 states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers real recordings; loadAllCorpora at lines 137-149 returns only those synthetic loaders.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve an operator selection\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.7 in epic.md:141 requires --resume to resolve the operator's selection. index.ts:210-226 only notifies the candidate list and returns the single candidate or null for multiple candidates; thread-resolution.test.ts:255-292 asserts fail-closed behavior for multiple candidates rather than a selected thread.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload identity reintroduced a PI custom-entry mapping contrary to the tech design\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md:22 says there is no PI-session-to-thread mapping to persist, and tech-design.md:26 says appendEntry is moot for mapping because no session-file pointer is written. index.ts:134-158 defines pi-lhc-thread-state, index.ts:304-306 reads it from ctx.sessionManager.getEntries(), index.ts:468-469 appends the current threadRef, and index.ts:677-679 wires that append through pi.appendEntry.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"NF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Configured gates pass\",\"evidence\":\"Ran pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify and pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all; both completed successfully with 20 test files and 143 tests passing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Local PI and pi-ai type declarations are temporary boundaries\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts declares the consumed PI API slice because the real package is not a workspace dependency; packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts provides local pi-ai typing while model-call dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Derived-form reuse remains deferred but correctness is preserved\",\"evidence\":\"fork.ts seeds forked threads by replay and does not copy ready derived forms; AC-3.3 permits requeue when reuse safety cannot be proven.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Add real recorded PI corpora or formally narrow AC-6.1 before passing the epic.\",\"Human ruling or tech-design update needed for the PI custom-entry threadRef mapping introduced in index.ts.\",\"Human ruling or PI API change needed for --resume operator selection in production.\",\"If the custom-entry mapping is accepted, update the architecture docs and lifecycle tests so thread identity is consistently specified as registry threadId, including fork reload.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"0d11db1f-f468-43d3-9493-3363697017d9\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2, 4, 5, and 6 are mostly coherent: capture, turn derivation, fork replay, inference routing, and startup validation all run through connector entry points and real LHC surfaces.\",\"Story 1 thread identity drift remains material: the current code both adds a PI custom-entry thread pointer and still keeps a cwd-most-recent fallback, while the epic and tech design describe launch/registry resolution with no PI-session-to-thread mapping.\",\"Story 3 does not meet the epic-level verification contract because the corpus loaders are synthetic stand-ins rather than recorded PI corpora.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Epic 1 correctly remains observe-only: index.ts registers no context hook and capture does not alter what PI serves to the model.\",\"The converter architecture matches the tech design: map-message is pure, turn-accumulator owns the LHC turn boundary, and converter writes through intakeStream.messageEvents.\",\"The current reload implementation conflicts with the tech design resolution of I-1/I-7: tech-design.md says there is no stored PI-session-to-thread pointer, but index.ts writes and reads a pi-lhc-thread-state custom entry via appendEntry/sessionManager.\",\"The production --resume default does not resolve an operator selection. It notifies the candidate list, auto-resolves only one candidate, and returns null for multiple candidates.\",\"Fork seeding uses the real intake path and source read-back is not written, but the fork path uses a filePath ThreadRef for the target, which is another sign that lifecycle thread identity is not consistently registry-id based.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Flow 1 is incomplete against the written architecture and AC-1.7: launch resolution exists, but reload identity and resume selection still require human ruling or design update.\",\"Flow 2 is covered by source and tests: ordered message mapping, turn derivation, runtime notes, idempotency, gaps, parallel tools, errors, and aborts are implemented.\",\"Flow 3 is implemented with replay seeding and derived-form requeue; source immutability is covered.\",\"Flow 4 is implemented through createModelCall over PI modelRegistry plus pi-ai dynamic import, with classified failures and closed-loop persisted outcomes covered.\",\"Flow 5 is implemented: assignments load defaults/overrides, startup validation reports unreachable lanes, and capture continues.\",\"Flow 6 is not fully covered: replay is deterministic and compares real read-back, but it consumes synthetic fixtures instead of recorded PI corpora required by AC-6.1.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapter was found in src capture/fork/inspect paths: capture uses real LHC intakeStream, fork replay uses intakeStream.messageEvents, and inspect reads real LHC surfaces.\",\"Test-only model fakes are confined to test/fixtures and are not production code.\",\"createModelCall does not fabricate output when pi-ai is missing; it returns a classified failure.\",\"Material non-real verification path: packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts explicitly says loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers recordings, so Flow 6 is not proving recorded PI corpus replay.\",\"Material architecture drift: production index.ts persists threadRef in PI custom entries, despite tech-design.md stating the mapping persistence problem is dissolved and no session-file pointer is written.\",\"Material resume limitation: production defaultSelectThread has no interactive operator selection path for multiple cwd-scoped threads.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Capture verification uses synthetic stand-ins instead of recorded PI corpora\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:69 and epic.md:229-231 require recorded corpora replay through the converter. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-5 states the loaders build synthetic stand-ins until M0 delivers real recordings; loadAllCorpora at lines 137-149 returns only those synthetic loaders.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve an operator selection\",\"evidence\":\"AC-1.7 in epic.md:141 requires --resume to resolve the operator's selection. index.ts:210-226 only notifies the candidate list and returns the single candidate or null for multiple candidates; thread-resolution.test.ts:255-292 asserts fail-closed behavior for multiple candidates rather than a selected thread.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload identity reintroduced a PI custom-entry mapping contrary to the tech design\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md:22 says there is no PI-session-to-thread mapping to persist, and tech-design.md:26 says appendEntry is moot for mapping because no session-file pointer is written. index.ts:134-158 defines pi-lhc-thread-state, index.ts:304-306 reads it from ctx.sessionManager.getEntries(), index.ts:468-469 appends the current threadRef, and index.ts:677-679 wires that append through pi.appendEntry.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"NF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Configured gates pass\",\"evidence\":\"Ran pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify and pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all; both completed successfully with 20 test files and 143 tests passing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Local PI and pi-ai type declarations are temporary boundaries\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts declares the consumed PI API slice because the real package is not a workspace dependency; packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts provides local pi-ai typing while model-call dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Derived-form reuse remains deferred but correctness is preserved\",\"evidence\":\"fork.ts seeds forked threads by replay and does not copy ready derived forms; AC-3.3 permits requeue when reuse safety cannot be proven.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Add real recorded PI corpora or formally narrow AC-6.1 before passing the epic.\",\"Human ruling or tech-design update needed for the PI custom-entry threadRef mapping introduced in index.ts.\",\"Human ruling or PI API change needed for --resume operator selection in production.\",\"If the custom-entry mapping is accepted, update the architecture docs and lifecycle tests so thread identity is consistently specified as registry threadId, including fork reload.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[{\"code\":\"PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID\",\"message\":\"Provider output was invalid for claude-code.\",\"detail\":\"Provider stdout was not exact JSON.; raw stdout bytes=1930233; raw stdout preview=\\\"{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"system\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"subtype\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"init\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"cwd\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"54bb6891-be78-43f8-a277-229ffe48e3f0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Task\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AskUserQuestion\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Bash\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"CronCreate\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"CronDelete\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"CronList\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Edit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"EnterPlanMode\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"EnterWorktree\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ExitPlanMode\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ExitWorktree\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"NotebookEdit\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Read\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"ScheduleWakeup\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Skill\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TaskCreate\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TaskGet\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TaskList\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TaskOutput\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TaskStop\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TaskUpdate\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"WebFetch\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"WebSearch\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Workflow\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Write\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"mcp_servers\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-opus-4-8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"p...[truncated]\\\"; stdout log=/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/streams/003-epic-review.stdout.log; stderr log=/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/streams/003-epic-review.stderr.log\"}],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/epic/003-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:47:13.586Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T13:51:05.192Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:41:- Test fixture and corpus-loading harness that can load recorded PI corpora and expected intake-event shapes.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:93:| Fixtures | `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/thread.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:165:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:204:| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:211:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:301:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:324:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:402:    planSummary: \"Built the pi-lhc walking skeleton (Epic 1 Chunk 0, tdd-lite, observe-only). Scaffolded the package (package.json with lhc workspace dep + verification-tier scripts, tsconfig/tsconfig.test mirroring lhc, vitest config, and zero-dep lint/boundaries/immutability scripts incl. a new connector-specific check-boundaries.mjs enforcing pinned cross-surface import edges for lifecycle/capture/inference/verify with no cycle). Declared the PI v0.79.2 extension surface locally in src/pi/types.ts (the @earendil-works PI packages are not installed in this workspace) from the verified wiring research. src/index.ts registers exactly the 9-hook Epic 1 observe-only rail (NOT context) via activate(pi)/createConnector(), with guarded handlers that never throw into PI and retain only plain data. lifecycle/state.ts is complete plain-data SessionState (the anti-stale-ctx shape) + createSessionState; every other module is a typed fail-closed stub per the tech-design Interface Definitions — pure algorithms (mapMessage, eventKey, TurnAccumulator, classifyFailure, detectFork, validateReachable, report, loadAssignments) throw NotImplementedError, services (initInstance, resolveThread, pickThread, capture, seedFork) return an LHC not_implemented OpResult, createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other' failure, and replayCorpus returns matches:false — no stub reports success. initLhc is provided as the createSdk rename (A-4). Test fixtures: corpus loader (5 named lifecycles) with a real validateCorpus shape/coherence checker + makeTruncatedCorpus, synthetic PI/intake builders, deterministic ModelCall fakes, and a real temp-SQLite-thread factory. 6 foundation test files / 19 tests cover corpus validity (+ invalid builder rejected), synthetic coherence, ModelCall fakes, temp-thread create+reopen, hook-rail registration + fail-closed/plain-data handlers + init/dispose seam, and verification-config presence.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:489:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:504:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:524:        - \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:559:      - \"Q3 (tech design): M0 recorded-corpora breadth — the corpus loaders build synthetic stand-ins for the 5 named lifecycles and the machinery widens as real recordings arrive (Story 3).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:560:      - \"Q1/A-7 (tech design): image/file-reference intake handling is an M0 decision; the safe interim is degrade-to-runtime_note, which the converter implements in Story 2.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"cdabf308-0529-4edb-9c42-8bdcdceb167e\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5d0-02af-7833-aa10-b5a891cf7379\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5d0-02af-7833-aa10-b5a891cf7379\",\"storyId\":\"03-capture-verification\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-capture-verification\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Capture Verification\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/03-capture-verification.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/converter.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 3 against AC-6.1 through AC-6.3, the replay harness, corpus fixtures, verification tests, inspect/health evidence, and configured gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay does not compare actual message and turn read-back records\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 requires the thread read-back — events, messages, and turns — to match fixture expectations. `replayCorpus` reads `intakeStream.listEvents` and `inspect.overview` only (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:282-291`). `compareReadback` compares event kind/payload order, then checks only `overview.messages.visible`, `overview.messages.byKind`, `overview.turns.closed`, and `overview.turns.open` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:219-260`). The SDK exposes actual message and turn read-back surfaces (`messages` and `turns` exports in `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:1-4`, plus `MessageRecord`/`TurnRecord` types at `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:173-182`), but the Story 3 harness and tests do not consume them. `test/verify/replay.test.ts` adds an extra TC-6.1 assertion for event kinds only (`packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts:86-91`). This leaves message content/order/turn association unverified despite the AC naming messages and turns explicitly.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Corpus replay uses synthetic flat messages and inferred lifecycle instead of recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Replay does not compare actual message and turn read-back records\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 requires the thread read-back — events, messages, and turns — to match fixture expectations. `replayCorpus` reads `intakeStream.listEvents` and `inspect.overview` only (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:282-291`). `compareReadback` compares event kind/payload order, then checks only `overview.messages.visible`, `overview.messages.byKind`, `overview.turns.closed`, and `overview.turns.open` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:219-260`). The SDK exposes actual message and turn read-back surfaces (`messages` and `turns` exports in `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:1-4`, plus `MessageRecord`/`TurnRecord` types at `packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:173-182`), but the Story 3 harness and tests do not consume them. `test/verify/replay.test.ts` adds an extra TC-6.1 assertion for event kinds only (`packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts:86-91`). This leaves message content/order/turn association unverified despite the AC naming messages and turns explicitly.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Corpus replay uses synthetic flat messages and inferred lifecycle instead of recorded PI hook corpora\",\"evidence\":\"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-6.2 / TC-6.2: deterministic replay and same-thread re-replay are covered by `test/verify/replay.test.ts`; full `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed with 79 tests.\",\"AC-6.3 / TC-6.3: inspect overview/health counts, last event span, capture gaps, and failed derivations are covered by `test/verify/replay.test.ts`; full `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed.\",\"Fixture validity risk for current fixture shapes: `test/fixtures/corpus.test.ts` validates well-formed expected event shapes and rejects a malformed corpus.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1: actual `messages.listMessages` and `turns.listTurns` read-back records are not compared to fixture expectations.\",\"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1: recorded PI corpus lifecycle replay is not proven; current corpus sources are synthetic flat `AgentMessage[]` inputs with inferred boundaries.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\",\"result\":\"fail\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts` synthesizes entry ids and agent-run boundaries instead of replaying recorded hook lifecycle events, so the verification path is not yet proving recorded-corpus fidelity.\",\"`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts` does not use the real message and turn read-back surfaces, only overview counts for those sections.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[\"If M0 recorded corpora are still unavailable, does the impl lead want to explicitly accept synthetic stand-ins for this story, or should Story 3 remain blocked until those fixture inputs exist?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Configured story gate `pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify` passed. `green-verify` failed only at `check-test-immutability.mjs` for four pre-existing Story 2 capture test files, matching the implementor's reported drift and not the configured Story 3 gate.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:06:44.123Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T11:11:24.963Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/010-implementor.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"641da93d-439c-483a-a286-4926884c92e6\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-8\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"fc8b0d70-702e-4abc-9faa-dda18cc81eaf\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"fc8b0d70-702e-4abc-9faa-dda18cc81eaf\",\"storyId\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution\",\"title\":\"Story 1: Session Lifecycle and Thread Resolution\"},\"planSummary\":\"Fresh consolidating implement for Story 1 (session lifecycle + launch-driven thread resolution) on the recovered on-disk code, resolving verifier findings SV-001/002/003 and the A-8 LHC registry additions the launch modes depend on. SV-001 (production placeholder): activate() now resolves/creates the thread and initializes one real background LHC instance on session_start; the --resume default selector resolves the most-recent cwd thread (not null); production-path tests (TC-1.1/1.2/1.7) drive the real defaults with only environment overrides, not an injected SDK config/selector. As the completion of SV-001 I replaced the deterministic provider in the production default config — which the LHC SDK documents as 'selectable only by explicit name — never a production default' — with a fail-closed observeOnlyProvider whose seven ops each return a non-retryable failure; it satisfies construction without fabricating derived forms, is never invoked in Story 1 (no capture and no work handlers means no derivation work is queued), and is replaced by the real PI-auth-backed inference config in Stories 5/6. SV-002 (reload durability): the resolved thread id is held at module scope so it survives the extension teardown a reload performs; the reload test now discards connector A entirely and reconstructs with a FRESH connector B from that durable id with no launch flag and no duplicate thread, a complementary test proves a non-reload teardown clears the memory (so the next no-flag session is a new thread), and the restart-risk resolver test reconstructs purely by resolving the durable id from the registry after discarding all in-memory state. SV-003 (missing title): new threads are registered with cwd plus defaultThreadTitle(cwd) (the cwd leaf), asserted in TC-1.1, a dedicated resolver test, and the reload test. A-8 LHC registry work (packages/lhc): a cwd column via registry migration v2 with migrate-on-read so a pre-cwd v1 registry upgrades lazily; partial-id (prefix) resolve with exact-match-wins, ambiguous_thread_id on >1 and thread_not_found on 0 (never creates); LIKE-metacharacter escaping so '_'/'%' in ids match literally; a cwd filter enforced as the SQL WHERE clause (anti-shim, not a post-filter); and deterministic ORDER BY created_at, rowid for most-recent. The connector retains only plain-data SessionState plus the live LhcInstance (held in the closure, excluded from the snapshot); drainSettled is called only from dispose (the flush), never from session_start, so the connector never drives the queue.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/shared/errors.ts\",\"reason\":\"Add the ambiguous_thread_id caller-error code for A-8 partial-id resolve ambiguity.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/registry.ts\",\"reason\":\"A-8: cwd column via registry migration v2; migrate-on-read in openRegistryForRead so a pre-cwd v1 registry upgrades on open; cwd in the row type/insert/selects; selectThreadRowsByPrefix (LIKE-metachar-escaped, ESCAPE '\\\\\\\\') for partial-id; cwd-filter parameter on selectAllThreadRows enforced as a WHERE clause; deterministic ORDER BY created_at, rowid.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"A-8: NewThreadInput.cwd + ThreadInfo.cwd stored/returned; resolve does exact-then-prefix matching (ambiguous_thread_id on >1, thread_not_found on 0, never creates); cwd filter on listThreads.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: 11 registry-boundary tests for A-8 (cwd round-trip, no-cwd undefined, unique/ambiguous/absent partial-id, LIKE-metachar literal match, cwd-scoped list, empty cwd, most-recent ordering, v1->v2 migrate-on-read).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\",\"reason\":\"Implement initInstance (validate the thread via threads.info, force mode:background, wrap with a flush-on-dispose seam) and disposeInstance (null-safe no-op); dispose flushes via sdk.drainSettled (AC-1.1, AC-1.4, AC-1.5).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"reason\":\"Implement resolveThread (no-flag new with cwd+defaultThreadTitle title [SV-003], --session full+partial, --continue most-recent; unresolvable/ambiguous return the registry error, never a silent new thread), defaultThreadTitle, parseLaunchFlags(argv), and threadRefById/registryArg helpers (AC-1.2, AC-1.5, AC-1.6).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"reason\":\"Implement pickThread: cwd-scoped listThreads (the scope is the registry query, anti-shim) -> title+created choices -> injected selection -> resolve; empty cwd and cancellation return null without failing (AC-1.7).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"Connector wiring: session_start -> resolveForLaunch -> initInstance (real production defaults); session_before_switch/session_shutdown -> dispose(flush); reload reconstructs from the module-scope durable thread id (survives connector teardown), cleared on non-reload teardown. Replaced the deterministic provider in the production default config with a fail-closed observeOnlyProvider (SV-001 completion); --resume default selector resolves most-recent; plain-data snapshot + getInstance test seam.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: TC-1.1 (no-flag session_start with production defaults creates one cwd/title thread + one background instance, queue not driven) and TC-1.4 (shutdown flush + reattach reads every pre-shutdown event).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: TC-1.6 (all launch modes; bad/ambiguous fail loud, no thread created), parseLaunchFlags mapping, no-flag title, TC-1.7 picker (cwd-scoped/titled/empty-safe), TC-1.5 restart-risk (resolve-by-durable-id after full discard), TC-1.2/1.7 production connector path, TC-1.3 plain-data across ctx replacement, and the reload-after-teardown pair (fresh connector reconstructs; non-reload teardown clears memory).\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Update the Story 0 init/dispose stub block to the now-real fail-closed seam: init on a missing thread returns thread_not_found (no throw); dispose(null) is a successful no-op. Plain-data and hook-rail smoke unchanged.\"},{\"path\":\"packages/pi-lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"NEW: freeze the two Story 1 Red-phase lifecycle test files for green-verify's check-test-immutability.\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts: TC-1.1, TC-1.4 (2 cases)\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts: TC-1.6, parseLaunchFlags, no-flag-title, TC-1.7 (picker), TC-1.5 (restart-risk), TC-1.2, TC-1.7 (production), TC-1.3, TC-1.5 (reload fresh-connector), non-reload-clears (10 cases)\",\"packages/lhc/test/threads-a8.test.ts: A-8 cwd/partial-id/ambiguity/LIKE-escaping/cwd-scoped-list/most-recent/migrate-on-read (11 cases)\"],\"modified\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/test/smoke/extension-load.test.ts: init/dispose stub block rewritten to assert the real fail-closed seam (case count unchanged)\"],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":384,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":3},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"SV-001 (production path placeholder): activate()'s production default is a real construction-valid SDK config and session_start resolves/creates the thread and initializes a real background instance; the --resume default selector resolves the most-recent cwd thread instead of null; TC-1.1/1.2/1.7 exercise the real defaults with only environment overrides, not an injected SDK config or selector.\",\"SV-001 completion: replaced createDeterministicProvider() in the production default — which lhc documents as 'never a production default' — with a fail-closed observeOnlyProvider (seven ops each return {ok:false, retryable:false}); it satisfies construction without fabricating derived forms and is never invoked in Story 1 (no capture and an empty work-handler map mean no derivation work is queued).\",\"SV-002 (reload durability): the resolved thread id is held at module scope so it survives the connector teardown a reload performs; the reload test now discards connector A and reconstructs with a FRESH connector B (no flag, no duplicate); a complementary test proves a non-reload teardown clears the memory; the restart-risk resolver test reconstructs purely by resolving the durable id from the registry after discarding all in-memory state.\",\"SV-003 (missing title): new threads are registered with cwd plus defaultThreadTitle(cwd) (the cwd leaf), asserted in TC-1.1, a dedicated resolver test, and the reload test.\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"Anti-shim verified structurally: cwd scoping is a registry WHERE cwd = ? query (not a post-filter over an unscoped list), and the --session path returns the registry's thread_not_found/ambiguous_thread_id rather than ever falling through to newThread.\",\"Plain-data rule verified: SessionState holds only { threadRef, flags, health }; the live LhcInstance is held in the connector closure and excluded from snapshot(), so structuredClone(snapshot()) succeeds even though ctx/instance carry methods.\",\"observe-only preserved: with the fail-closed provider, no work handlers, and no capture in Story 1, the provider is never invoked, so no fabricated derivations can land; if a future change queued work before Stories 5/6 the provider fails closed rather than fabricating.\",\"drainSettled is called only from instance dispose (the flush), never from session_start, so the connector never drives the derivation queue (AC-1.1).\"]},\"openQuestions\":[\"Exact PI launch-flag spelling for the named-session mode: parseLaunchFlags handles --session/--session=, but recon notes mention --session-id; confirm against the real @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent dependency when it becomes a build dep (pi/types.ts is currently a local declaration).\",\"Production reload durable-id source: the module-scope id covers in-process reload (extension torn down, same process); --session/--continue/--resume re-resolve from the launch across process death; a no-flag session that suffers true process death relies on the launch re-resolving (most-recent is not guaranteed identical). The permanent home for reload lineage is LHC thread metadata (Feature 2+).\",\"Title derivation strategy (TDQ Q4): new threads use the cwd leaf as an interim, real, non-empty title; prompt-derived or operator-set titles are deferred.\",\"Interactive --resume operator picker awaits a PI input surface beyond ui.notify (verified v0.79.2 exposes only notify); the production default auto-resumes the most-recent cwd thread, and tests drive an explicit selection through the injected selector.\"],\"specDeviations\":[\"Local PI extension types in src/pi/types.ts (Story 0 accepted-risk, inherited): @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent and pi-ai are not yet build dependencies, so the connector declares the slice of the v0.79.2 contract it touches; reversible to the real imports when the dependency lands.\",\"initLhc is a thin wrapper over LHC's createSdk (Story 0 accepted, spec-anticipated by tech-arch A-4 / tech-design Q2; mechanical).\",\"resolveThread/pickThread signatures finalized to take injected deps ({ cwd, registryPath?, newThreadFilePath, newThreadTitle? } / { registryPath?, select }) rather than the interface sketch's (launch, pi: ExtensionAPI) / (cwd): ExtensionAPI carries neither cwd, the per-operation registryPath, a new-thread file path, nor a selection surface, so resolution takes injected deps (testable against a temp registry, defaulting to ~/.lhc in production).\",\"--resume is routed in index.ts to picker.pickThread while resolveThread owns new/--session/--continue (a UI-vs-registry separation), rather than resolveThread handling all four modes as the sketch implied.\",\"Story-1 production inference is a fail-closed observeOnlyProvider placeholder — NOT the deterministic provider (lhc: 'never a production default') and NOT the real inference config. The real PI-model-registry-backed inference (ModelCall + the seven assignments) is Stories 5/6, and @earendil-works/pi-ai is not yet a build dependency.\",\"New threads are created with cwd plus a default title equal to the cwd leaf directory name; prompt-derived/operator-set title derivation is deferred (TDQ Q4).\",\"A-8 LHC additions land in this story's scope (spec-anticipated by the story's Scope In and tech-design): ambiguous_thread_id added to the lhc ErrorCode set, and a registry v2 migration adds the cwd column with migrate-on-read for existing registries.\",\"The production --resume selector auto-resumes the most-recent cwd thread rather than presenting an interactive operator picker, because the locally-typed PI UI surface exposes only ui.notify; the picker machinery (cwd-scoped, titled, empty-safe, selection-resolving) is real and tested via an injected selection.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Proceed to Story 2 (Event Capture and Turn Derivation): build the converter (map-message fan-out, turn-accumulator deriving one LHC turn_end at agent_end, idempotency keys, batch flush with capture-failure isolation) on the lifecycle/instance seam landed here. Separately, when @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent + pi-ai become build dependencies, confirm the launch-flag spelling and reload semantics against live PI and replace the observeOnlyProvider placeholder with the real inference config in Stories 5/6.\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/010-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T05:23:10.925Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T05:37:40.607Z\"}\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/abort.test.ts:13:} from \"../fixtures/synthetic.js\";\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/011-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"6f89c00b-4771-418a-9dac-abfc7ddd30bd\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5f5-8cee-73a3-a1df-64da125e5d08\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec5f5-8cee-73a3-a1df-64da125e5d08\",\"storyId\":\"04-fork-as-new-thread\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"04-fork-as-new-thread\",\"title\":\"Story 4: Fork as New Thread\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/stories/04-fork-as-new-thread.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:331\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:565\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:80\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/test-plan.md:168\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on the two remaining Story 4 blockers and directly touched fork surfaces. Both prior findings are resolved, focused tests pass, and configured story/epic gates pass.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-002\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts:29-47 now reads previousSessionFile entries, compares previous entry ids against current session entries, and checks parentId links to previous ids. packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts:83-127 adds hook-absent fallback coverage with previousSessionFile plus current sessionManager entries carrying id/parentId chain evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"SV-04-005\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:325-342 now records diagnostics and returns on fork thread creation or instance init failure in the hook path. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:385-400 does the same in the fallback fork path. The normal launch fallthrough is gone for those fork setup failures.\"}],\"newFindings\":[],\"openFindings\":[],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1/TC-3.1: fork creates a new thread from session_before_fork hook data without depending on reason code, source event read-back remains unchanged, and hook-absent fallback is covered with session-tree id/parentId evidence.\",\"AC-3.2/TC-3.2: fork seeding replays source events through LHC intake to the target and focused tests verify seeded read-back through the fork point.\",\"AC-3.3/TC-3.3: v1 does not copy derived forms; focused tests show target work requeues pending, then derives ready independently.\"],\"unverified\":[]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"pass\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Focused fork suite passed: 1 file, 4 tests.\",\"Configured story gate passed: 16 files, 83 tests.\",\"Epic gate passed: 16 files, 83 tests.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/011-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-14T12:23:07.311Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-14T12:24:36.418Z\"}\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:184:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:223:| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:230:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:320:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/06-startup-validation-and-assignment-config/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:343:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\npackages/pi-lhc/test/capture/parallel-and-errors.test.ts:18:} from \"../fixtures/synthetic.js\";\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:41:- Test fixture and corpus-loading harness that can load recorded PI corpora and expected intake-event shapes.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:93:| Fixtures | `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/model-call.ts`, `packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/thread.ts` |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:165:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:204:| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:211:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:301:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:324:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:484:    planSummary: \"Built the pi-lhc walking skeleton (Epic 1 Chunk 0, tdd-lite, observe-only). Scaffolded the package (package.json with lhc workspace dep + verification-tier scripts, tsconfig/tsconfig.test mirroring lhc, vitest config, and zero-dep lint/boundaries/immutability scripts incl. a new connector-specific check-boundaries.mjs enforcing pinned cross-surface import edges for lifecycle/capture/inference/verify with no cycle). Declared the PI v0.79.2 extension surface locally in src/pi/types.ts (the @earendil-works PI packages are not installed in this workspace) from the verified wiring research. src/index.ts registers exactly the 9-hook Epic 1 observe-only rail (NOT context) via activate(pi)/createConnector(), with guarded handlers that never throw into PI and retain only plain data. lifecycle/state.ts is complete plain-data SessionState (the anti-stale-ctx shape) + createSessionState; every other module is a typed fail-closed stub per the tech-design Interface Definitions — pure algorithms (mapMessage, eventKey, TurnAccumulator, classifyFailure, detectFork, validateReachable, report, loadAssignments) throw NotImplementedError, services (initInstance, resolveThread, pickThread, capture, seedFork) return an LHC not_implemented OpResult, createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other' failure, and replayCorpus returns matches:false — no stub reports success. initLhc is provided as the createSdk rename (A-4). Test fixtures: corpus loader (5 named lifecycles) with a real validateCorpus shape/coherence checker + makeTruncatedCorpus, synthetic PI/intake builders, deterministic ModelCall fakes, and a real temp-SQLite-thread factory. 6 foundation test files / 19 tests cover corpus validity (+ invalid builder rejected), synthetic coherence, ModelCall fakes, temp-thread create+reopen, hook-rail registration + fail-closed/plain-data handlers + init/dispose seam, and verification-config presence.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:571:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:586:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:606:        - \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:641:      - \"Q3 (tech design): M0 recorded-corpora breadth — the corpus loaders build synthetic stand-ins for the 5 named lifecycles and the machinery widens as real recordings arrive (Story 3).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lea