reference/src-green-thread-events-v1/index.ts\\ndocs/key-insights/meta-thinking-and-tensions-braindump.md\\npackages/lhc/reference/src-green-thread-events-v1/token-counting/local-token-counter.ts\\npackages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\\ndocs/onboard/02-domain-design.md\\ndocs/onboard/01-core-concepts.md\\n\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:439:    planSummary: \"Built the pi-lhc walking skeleton (Epic 1 Chunk 0, tdd-lite, observe-only). Scaffolded the package (package.json with lhc workspace dep + verification-tier scripts, tsconfig/tsconfig.test mirroring lhc, vitest config, and zero-dep lint/boundaries/immutability scripts incl. a new connector-specific check-boundaries.mjs enforcing pinned cross-surface import edges for lifecycle/capture/inference/verify with no cycle). Declared the PI v0.79.2 extension surface locally in src/pi/types.ts (the @earendil-works PI packages are not installed in this workspace) from the verified wiring research. src/index.ts registers exactly the 9-hook Epic 1 observe-only rail (NOT context) via activate(pi)/createConnector(), with guarded handlers that never throw into PI and retain only plain data. lifecycle/state.ts is complete plain-data SessionState (the anti-stale-ctx shape) + createSessionState; every other module is a typed fail-closed stub per the tech-design Interface Definitions — pure algorithms (mapMessage, eventKey, TurnAccumulator, classifyFailure, detectFork, validateReachable, report, loadAssignments) throw NotImplementedError, services (initInstance, resolveThread, pickThread, capture, seedFork) return an LHC not_implemented OpResult, createModelCall returns a fail-closed 'other' failure, and replayCorpus returns matches:false — no stub reports success. initLhc is provided as the createSdk rename (A-4). Test fixtures: corpus loader (5 named lifecycles) with a real validateCorpus shape/coherence checker + makeTruncatedCorpus, synthetic PI/intake builders, deterministic ModelCall fakes, and a real temp-SQLite-thread factory. 6 foundation test files / 19 tests cover corpus validity (+ invalid builder rejected), synthetic coherence, ModelCall fakes, temp-thread create+reopen, hook-rail registration + fail-closed/plain-data handlers + init/dispose seam, and verification-config presence.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:526:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:541:        path: \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:561:        - \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:596:      - \"Q3 (tech design): M0 recorded-corpora breadth — the corpus loaders build synthetic stand-ins for the 5 named lifecycles and the machinery widens as real recordings arrive (Story 3).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:597:      - \"Q1/A-7 (tech design): image/file-reference intake handling is an M0 decision; the safe interim is degrade-to-runtime_note, which the converter implements in Story 2.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:667:      - \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:668:      - \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/synthetic.test.ts\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:713:        - \"S0-FIXTURE-HARNESS: corpus, synthetic, model-call, and temp-thread fixtures exist; corpus validation rejects malformed fixtures; temp-thread tests create and reopen real SQLite-backed LHC threads.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/00-foundation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-004.md:731:      - \"`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts` currently builds synthetic stand-ins for the named corpora. I treated that as non-blocking for Story 0 because `team-impl-log.md` records M0 real recorded corpus breadth as Story 3 fixture scope.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:27:Verify capture by replaying recorded PI corpora through the converter and matching deterministic thread read-back and inspect surfaces.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:45:- Creating M0 corpora. This story consumes M0 corpora as fixtures.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:49:**Dependencies:** Story 2. M0 corpora are fixture inputs.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:54:**AC-6.1:** Replaying a recorded PI corpus through the converter produces a thread whose read-back — events, messages, and turns — matches the fixture's expectation, including the chatty, tool-heavy, parallel-tool, error-result, and aborted-turn corpora.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:71:Story 3 is the proof layer for capture. It replays recorded PI corpora through the real converter and LHC intake path, then compares the thread read-back without serving context to a model.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:84:- M0 corpora breadth determines final fixture coverage; the replay machinery should widen as corpora arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:153:- Fixture replay compares events, messages, and turns for all available M0 corpora.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:170:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:209:| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:216:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:306:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:329:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 corpora; widens as they arrive.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:442:        title: \"Corpus replay uses synthetic flat messages and inferred lifecycle instead of recorded PI hook corpora\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:443:        evidence: \"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:470:        title: \"Corpus replay uses synthetic flat messages and inferred lifecycle instead of recorded PI hook corpora\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:471:        evidence: \"AC-6.1 is scoped to replaying recorded PI corpora. The fixture loader states that, until M0 delivers recordings, it builds synthetic stand-ins (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:1-4`), and each named corpus source is an in-memory `AgentMessage[]` built with `makeUserMessage` / `makeAssistantMessage` (`packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/corpus.ts:21-29`, `42-53`, `69-83`, `97-105`, `118-124`). The replay harness source type is also just `AgentMessage[]` (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:35-38`). During replay it synthesizes deterministic entry ids and infers `agent_end` boundaries from a new user prompt or end-of-stream (`packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:117-143`) instead of consuming recorded `message_end` / `agent_end` events with their original positions. That proves the converter on synthetic message shapes, but not replay fidelity for recorded PI corpora or recorded lifecycle ordering.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:488:        - \"AC-6.1 / TC-6.1: recorded PI corpus lifecycle replay is not proven; current corpus sources are synthetic flat `AgentMessage[]` inputs with inferred boundaries.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:505:      - \"If M0 recorded corpora are still unavailable, does the impl lead want to explicitly accept synthetic stand-ins for this story, or should Story 3 remain blocked until those fixture inputs exist?\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:589:        - \"replay derives agent-run (agent_end) boundaries from the source message stream (a new user prompt closes the prior run) because Corpus.source is a flat AgentMessage[] with no explicit run markers. This reconstruction is validated against every fixture's expected turn_end (the compare fails loudly if wrong). If M0 recordings encode explicit run/agent_end boundaries, driveCorpus should consume those instead of inferring them.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/03-capture-verification/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:591:      - \"M0 corpora breadth: the five synthetic corpora stand in until M0 delivers real PI recordings; the replay machinery is real and widens automatically as named corpora arrive (CORPUS_LOADERS / loadAllCorpora).\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:171:This plan maps every TC to one or more tests, assigns each to a chunk, and lays out the Red/Green sequence per chunk. The mock boundary is fixed by the tech design: the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall` (a deterministic fake) are the only external edges; everything LHC runs real against a temp SQLite thread. Connector modules are exercised through their entry points, never mocked against each other.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:210:| TC-1.6 | Launch modes resolve correctly | `launch` = `{}` / `{session:fullId}` / `{session:partialId}` / `{continue:true}` / `{session:badId}` | new creates; full+partial id resolve the right thread; continue resolves most-recent; bad id returns an actionable error and creates **no** thread |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:217:| TC-2.1 | User/assistant/toolResult record ordered; assistant fans out thinking→text→toolCall | synthetic sequence | events recorded in source order; assistant fan-out order exact |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:307:- **Red:** fixture-invariant tests (corpus shapes, synthetic coherence, temp-thread create+reopen); extension-loads smoke; package verification scripts/config present.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/04-fork-as-new-thread/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:330:- **Exit:** `green-verify`; 4 tests pass. Consumes M0 