{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 2, 4, 5, and 6 are broadly coherent: capture, turn derivation, fork replay, inference routing, and startup validation are wired through connector entry points and real LHC surfaces.\",\"Story 1 still has accepted-risk behavior that does not satisfy the literal epic contract: reload reattaches by cwd-most-recent for no-flag/resume launches, and production --resume cannot resolve an operator selection when more than one cwd thread exists.\",\"Story 3 does not meet the epic-level verification contract because the corpus fixtures are small handcrafted AgentMessage jsonl files, not recorded PI corpora with the real hook/lifecycle surface the epic requires.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The observe-only boundary is preserved: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts registers no context hook, and capture does not alter what PI sends to the model.\",\"The converter module shape matches the tech design: map-message is pure, turn-accumulator owns LHC turn close, and converter writes through intakeStream.messageEvents.\",\"Reload behavior drifts from AC-1.5 and tech-design.md: the design says reload reconstructs from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id, while packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts falls back to cwd-most-recent for no-flag and --resume reloads.\",\"The --resume production path has a picker abstraction, but the default selector only notifies and returns null for multiple candidates, so the production path does not resolve the operator's selection required by AC-1.7.\",\"A recorded-risk note exists in docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/team-impl-log.md, but the epic and tech design were not updated to narrow AC-1.5, AC-1.7, or AC-6.1.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Flow 1 is incomplete against the written contract: new/continue/session resolution exists, but reload exact-thread reconstruction and production resume selection are not fully implemented.\",\"Flow 2 is covered by source and tests: ordered message mapping, turn derivation, runtime notes, idempotency, capture gaps, parallel tools, errors, and aborts are implemented.\",\"Flow 3 is implemented with replay seeding and derived-form requeue; source thread immutability is covered.\",\"Flow 4 is implemented through createModelCall over PI modelRegistry plus pi-ai dynamic import, with failure classification and closed-loop persisted outcomes covered by tests using injected completion/model-call boundaries.\",\"Flow 5 is implemented: assignments load defaults/overrides, startup validation reports unreachable lanes, and capture continues.\",\"Flow 6 is incomplete: replay is deterministic and compares durable read-back, but it does not consume real recorded PI corpora as required by AC-6.1.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapter was found in src capture/fork/inspect paths: capture uses real LHC intakeStream, fork replay uses intakeStream.messageEvents, and inspect reads real LHC surfaces.\",\"Test-only model-call fakes are confined to packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures and are not production code.\",\"createModelCall does not fabricate output when pi-ai is unavailable; it returns a classified failure.\",\"Material non-real verification path: packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl are handcrafted AgentMessage rows, and packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:36-38 still describes the corpus source as synthetic stand-in data.\",\"Material production limitation: packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:192-200 defaultSelectThread presents candidates through notify but resolves only a single candidate; multiple candidates return null instead of a selected thread.\",\"Material reload limitation: packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141-147 resolves reload by cwd-most-recent, which is not durable resolved-thread-id reconstruction.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Capture verification does not use recorded PI corpora\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:229-231 requires recorded PI corpus replay, including chatty/tool-heavy/parallel-tool/error-result/aborted-turn corpora. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl contain handcrafted AgentMessage rows with no PI hook metadata or lifecycle events, and packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:36-38 still calls the source synthetic stand-in data.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/chatty.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/tool-heavy.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/parallel-tool.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/error-result.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/aborted-turn.jsonl\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/verify/replay.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-6.1\",\"TC-6.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve operator selection for multiple cwd threads\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:141 requires --resume to list cwd threads and resolve the operator's selection. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:192-200 notifies the candidate list but returns a thread only when there is exactly one candidate; packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255-292 asserts this fail-closed production behavior instead of a selected thread.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload can attach the wrong thread because it uses cwd-most-recent instead of the resolved threadId\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md:137 requires reload to reconstruct from durable state, the resolved thread id, and continue on the same thread. packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141-147 lists cwd threads and returns the last row for no-flag/--resume reloads. This only proves correct when no newer cwd thread exists, which is the narrow scenario covered by packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:336-373.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"NF-001\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Configured gates pass\",\"evidence\":\"Ran pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify and pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all; both completed successfully with 20 test files and 142 tests passing.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Local PI and pi-ai type declarations remain a runtime packaging boundary\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts declares the consumed PI API slice and packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts declares the pi-ai completion type because the real PI packages are not workspace dependencies; packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/model-call.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/package.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"NF-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Derived-form reuse remains deferred while fork correctness is preserved\",\"evidence\":\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts seeds forked threads by replay and does not copy ready derived forms; AC-3.3 permits requeue when reuse safety cannot be proven.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/fork.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.3\",\"TC-3.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Replace handcrafted corpus jsonl files with real recorded PI corpora or formally narrow AC-6.1 before passing the epic.\",\"Human ruling or spec update needed for production --resume behavior under PI v0.79.2 when multiple cwd threads exist.\",\"Human ruling or design update needed for exact reload thread identity without a PI-thread mapping record.\",\"If the accepted-risk lifecycle behavior stands, update epic.md and tech-design.md so AC-1.5 and AC-1.7 match the implementation and tests.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
