e reload and resume behaviors highlight significant architectural differences. Reviewer 2 identifies critical issues with thread resolution mechanisms. The reload process fails to reconstruct from the resolved thread ID, while the --resume function cannot handle multiple candidate threads effectively. These findings suggest fundamental misalignments with the original acceptance criteria.\n\nI'll investigate the implementation details to understand the discrepancy between reviewers' assessments, focusing on the specific implementation nuances that might explain the divergent conclusions.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a1de899-4d5a-4e8b-9eb8-54d1998ea0a6","uuid":"3f07cca1-3a5f-4134-8c83-559fd2acae14"}
