{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026061421561170434080a4d54584","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have sufficient context to produce the canonical epic review. Let me reconcile the independent reviewer findings against the codebase evidence.\n\n**Key Reconciliation Points:**\n\n1. **Corpus fixtures (EV-001 vs. EF-002)**: Both reviewers acknowledge M0 corpora are pending. The evidence confirms fixtures are synthetic (replay.ts line 36-38: \"synthetic PI source messages (the stand-in until M0 delivers recordings)\"). This is a documented M0 dependency, not a code defect.\n\n2. **Story 1 lifecycle deviations (EV-002, EV-003 vs. reviewer-1's silence)**: Reviewer 2 correctly identifies that production --resume fails closed for multiple candidates (index.ts lines 192-200) and reload uses cwd-most-recent (thread-resolution.ts lines 141-147). These were dispositioned as accepted-risk due to PI v0.79.2 lacking interactive input/selection API (team-impl-log lines 101-108).\n\n3. **LHC SDK exports (EF-001)**: sdk.ts exports FORM_KINDS (line 33) and WORK_KIND_REGISTRY (line 27). WORK_KIND_REGISTRY is in SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS (retirement.test.ts line 27), but FORM_KINDS is not—this discrepancy exists.\n\n4. **Gate status**: Both reviewers report pass—verify-all passes with 142 tests across 20 files.\n\nThe canonical outcome hinges on whether documented accepted-risk deviations should block epic closeout. The impl-lead approved these under standing authorization with upstream requests filed, but they remain material departures from the literal AC contract.```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"revise\",\n  \"reviewerLabels\": [\"epic-reviewer-1\", \"epic-reviewer-2\"],\n  \"reconciliationSummary\": \"Two reviewers reached different outcomes (revise vs. block) primarily over whether documented accepted-risk deviations should block epic closeout. Reviewer-1 (claude-code) treated Story 1's accepted-risk deviations (reload using cwd-most-recent, --resume failing closed for multiple candidates) as resolved via impl-lead ruling, surfacing only EF-001 as non-blocking. Reviewer-2 (codex) correctly identified that these are material departures from the literal AC contract (EV-002, EV-003) and that corpus fixtures are synthetic stand-ins rather than recorded PI corpora (EV-001). All three findings are supported by code evidence: index.ts lines 192-200 (defaultSelectThread returns null for multiple candidates), thread-resolution.ts lines 141-147 (reload uses cwd-most-recent), and replay.ts lines 36-38 (synthetic stand-in data). The team implementation log records these as approved accepted-risk deviations due to PI v0.79.2 API constraints and M0 dependency status. Both reviewers agreed gates pass (142 tests, 20 files). The canonical review confirms all three findings remain supported but recommends non-blocking given documented approvals and upstream requests.\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Stories 0-4 are complete with verified receipts in team-impl-log.md\",\n    \"Stories 5-6 (Inference Host Routing + Startup Validation) implemented and gated\",\n    \"Cross-story consistency maintained: plain-data-only state, converter architecture, and idempotency design align across stories\",\n    \"Capture spine (S0→S1→S2→S3) is strictly linear as designed\",\n    \"Fork (S4) and Inference (S5) branch correctly from the capture spine and lifecycle foundation\",\n    \"All configured gates pass: pi-lhc verify-all = 142 tests passing across 20 test files\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Turn-derivation contract (PI turn ≠ LHC turn) correctly implemented: TurnAccumulator ignores PI's per-step turn_end and emits exactly one LHC turn_end at agent_end\",\n    \"Converter follows tech design: map-message (pure) → turn-accumulator (stateful) → converter (orchestrates batch flush)\",\n    \"Idempotency uses 4-tier precedence system (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fingerprint) as specified\",\n    \"Fork detection uses both hook-based (session_before_fork) and session-tree fallback as Epic 1 design allows\",\n    \"Plain-data-only rule enforced: SessionState holds only threadRef and flags; no PI objects retained\",\n    \"Architecture-risk tests present: restart/reload, idempotency double-replay, adapter-boundary failure classification, atomicity isolation, source-vs-derived fork immutability\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"All 6 AC-sets (AC-1.1 through AC-6.3) have corresponding tests\",\n    \"Test coverage: 142 tests across 20 test files pass (pi-lhc verify-all)\",\n    \"Corpus replay tests consume synthetic fixtures pending M0 delivery; replay harness machinery is complete\",\n    \"Closed-loop test (TC-4.5) proves capture→derivation→recorded-outcome end-to-end through real scheduler + drainSettled\",\n    \"Architecture-risk tests cover: restart survival, idempotency dedup, adapter-boundary classification, atomicity isolation, source-vs-derived fork immutability\",\n    \"TC-6.1 (corpus replay) and TC-6.2 (deterministic re-replay) provide golden-case coverage against synthetic fixtures\",\n    \"Coverage gaps acknowledged: M0 corpus breadth pending; image/file-ref handling decision deferred (degrade-to-runtime_note interim in place)\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"pi-ai boundary is real: createModelCall dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai at runtime (model-call.ts lines 78-90), returning classified failure when unavailable—never fabricated text\",\n    \"Default assignments use real PI model (openai-codex/gpt-5.4 per PI v0.79.2 catalog), not placeholder\",\n    \"Test fixtures use deterministic ModelCall fakes (fakeModelCallText, fakeModelCallFailure, fakeModelCallRouter) at mock boundary as designed\",\n    \"Closed-loop test wires through real scheduler + drainSettled, not fake derivation path\",\n    \"Replay harness drives through real converter + intakeStream into temp SQLite threads, not mocked intake\",\n    \"Local PI type declarations (src/pi/types.ts, src/inference/pi-ai.ts) are documented deviation—verified mirror of v0.79.2 research, environmental necessity\",\n    \"initLhc wrapper over createSdk is spec-anticipated mechanical rename (tech-design A-4/Q2)\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EC-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Production --resume does not resolve operator selection for multiple cwd threads\",\n      \"evidence\": \"epic.md AC-1.7 requires --resume to list cwd threads and resolve operator's selection. packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:192-200 (defaultSelectThread) presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify but returns null for multiple candidates, directing operator to relaunch with --session. Test TC-1.7 (thread-resolution.test.ts:255-293) asserts this fail-closed behavior. Team impl-log records as accepted-risk due to PI v0.79.2 lacking interactive input/selection API; upstream request filed.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.7\", \"TC-1.7\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EC-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Reload can attach wrong thread because it uses cwd-most-recent instead of resolved threadId\",\n      \"evidence\": \"epic.md AC-1.5 requires reload to reconstruct from durable state (resolved thread id). packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141-147 (resolveReloadThread) returns cwd-most-recent for no-flag and --resume reloads. Test TC-1.5 (thread-resolution.test.ts:336-373) proves correct only when no newer cwd thread exists. Team impl-log records as accepted-risk; design forbids PI-session→thread mapping and PI lacks extension API for exact thread recovery.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\",\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.5\", \"TC-1.5\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EF-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"LHC verify fails due to FORM_KINDS not in SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS list\",\n      \"evidence\": \"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts:33 exports FORM_KINDS, but packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts:20-49 (SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS) does not include it. WORK_KIND_REGISTRY is correctly listed at line 27. This causes retirement.test.ts:62 to fail when checking export list equality.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/lhc/test/retirement.test.ts\", \"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"LHC-Epic-05-TC-6.1\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"same-session-implementor\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EF-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Capture verification uses synthetic corpus fixtures pending M0 delivery\",\n      \"evidence\": \"epic.md AC-6.1 requires replaying recorded PI corpora. packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl contain handcrafted AgentMessage data. packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts:36-38 comment states 'synthetic PI source messages (the stand-in until M0 delivers recordings)'. Team impl-log records Story 3 accepted with M0 inputs pending; fixture breadth will widen as corpora arrive.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md\", \"packages/pi-lhc/test/fixtures/pi-corpora/*.jsonl\", \"packages/pi-lhc/src/verify/replay.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-6.1\", \"TC-6.1\", \"A-2\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EF-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Local PI type declarations remain pending package installation\",\n      \"evidence\": \"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts and packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts declare local types instead of importing from @earendil-works packages (not yet installed in workspace). Team impl-log records as accepted-risk with documented plan to swap to real imports when @earendil-works packages installed (Epic 2/4 packaging).\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\", \"packages/pi-lhc/src/inference/pi-ai.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"Story-0-deviation-1\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EF-004\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"initLhc→createSdk rename pending in LHC package\",\n      \"evidence\": \"initLhc is thin wrapper over createSdk. Tech-design A-4/Q2 notes this as spec-anticipated mechanical rename. Team impl-log records as pending mechanical change.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/instance.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"A-4\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Human ruling or spec update for production --resume behavior under PI v0.79.2 when multiple cwd threads exist (EC-001)\",\n    \"Human ruling or design update for exact reload thread identity without PI-thread mapping record (EC-002)\",\n    \"Replace handcrafted corpus jsonl files with real recorded PI corpora or formally narrow AC-6.1 before epic closeout (EF-002)\",\n    \"Add FORM_KINDS to SDK_ONLY_EXPORTS in retirement.test.ts (EF-001)\",\n    \"createSdk→initLhc rename in LHC package (mechanical, A-4)\",\n    \"Local PI type declarations swap to real imports when @earendil-works packages installed (Epic 2/4)\",\n    \"PI extension input/selection API for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload (upstream request filed)\",\n    \"M0 decision A-7: image/file-reference handling (placeholder vs intake-schema extension); degrade-to-runtime_note interim in place\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a1de899-4d5a-4e8b-9eb8-54d1998ea0a6","uuid":"d1776a91-5efa-4f1c-9d65-da32f745c820"}
